module engine where

-- =========================================================================
-- validation-observe.fenel — the quantified-OBSERVATION fence (signature-
-- substrate Phase 4+4b, slice 3b; P4-D2's SECOND deliverable).
--
-- WHAT THIS IS FOR. Slice 3a landed the rigid atom κ: a prenex rank-1 scheme
-- `∀a. τ` is validated by replacing each quantified variable with ONE fresh
-- rigid and checking the body against that single instance. The soundness
-- statement is WHOLE-EXECUTION SUBSTITUTION EQUIVARIANCE — replacing each κᵢ
-- throughout an accepted derivation with any well-kinded ground τᵢ must
-- preserve type-correct execution, including wrapper behaviour, target
-- selection, effects/context, and calls.
--
-- WHY A FENCE IS NEEDED AT ALL. Fenel is WEAK-∀, not parametric-∀. Values
-- carry their type at runtime and the substrate observes it: `typeOf`, the
-- four `is*` shape predicates, `$tag` discrimination, `truthy`, structural
-- `eq`, and — deepest of all — instance selection by the runtime type of a
-- dispatch argument (`rsvTypeKey`, dispatch.fenel:163). A body that OBSERVES a
-- κ-typed value can behave differently at two ground instantiations, so its
-- single-instance derivation does not generalize.
--
-- NON-OBSERVATION IS A SUFFICIENT CONDITION, NOT A DEFINITION. This module
-- decides a CONSERVATIVE sufficient condition for equivariance. It is
-- DELIBERATELY INCOMPLETE: a type observer can return different Booleans at
-- different instantiations and still inhabit `∀a. a -> Boolean`. Rejecting it
-- is a defensible weak-∀ policy — it is NOT a claim that such a body "is not
-- polymorphic". A reader who thinks this fence CHARACTERIZES polymorphism will
-- try to "fix" the incompleteness; do not.
--
-- AND IT IS SUFFICIENT ONLY IF THE BOUNDARY IS COMPLETE. The condition covers
-- raw evaluator forms and wrappers, ACTIVE runtime implementation selection,
-- every κ-typed binder AND intermediate result, and callee summaries with
-- exact instantiation. Named theorem dependencies fenced ELSEWHERE, not here:
-- dependent `$el` (`RsnDependentEl`), qualified and bare capability dispatch
-- with no scope snapshot (`RsnScopeDependentDispatch` at the parent's own
-- gate), effects/`requires` (`RsnEffectfulScEff`), captures
-- (`RsnCapture`), higher-rank use and unsupported syntax
-- (`RsnUnsupportedRankOrKind` / `RsnUnsupportedSyntax`). LAWS DO NOT
-- SUBSTITUTE: `Reprable`'s round-trip laws (std/interfaces.fenel:584-589) bind
-- `lift`/`lower` to a perf branch; they do NOT show that representation
-- inspection is parametric.
--
-- THE CARRIER IS THE RAW BODY, AND THE `Pattern` ADT IS *NOT* THE BOUND. The
-- runtime matcher `matchPattern` (json-logic.ts:1793-1861) accepts an
-- ARBITRARY object, honours `$bind`, and performs structural object/array
-- matching with a KEY-PRESENCE requirement. An analysis founded on the
-- four-case surface `Pattern` ADT would answer "no reflection" for bodies that
-- reflect — the exact defect class this fence exists to prevent. So the
-- classifier is founded on an exhaustive transfer table over the COMPLETE raw
-- evaluator form set (`evaluate`'s TWELVE return arms — one of which is the
-- `KNOWN_OPS` arm, expanding into all forty ops, and the other ELEVEN of which
-- group into NINE non-op transfer classes — plus `matchPattern`'s six arms),
-- and ANY form without a row FENCES. The counts are stated exactly because a
-- wrong count in the prose beside a hand-maintained list is how the
-- hand-maintained half rots; slice 3d re-derives the arm inventory from source
-- so the count cannot drift silently (see `obs.form.arms`).
--
-- RELATION TO THE SLICE-2b LEDGER. This shares the raw traversal SKELETON with
-- `validation-ledger.fenel` and never clones it: the ledger deliberately
-- treats patterns as inert (it collects binders, never rows) and models NO
-- value flow, which is precisely what an observation fence must model.
--
-- VOCABULARY IS REUSED, NOT REINVENTED. Every fence here is an existing
-- `ValidationReason` (validation.fenel:40-63) and every path segment an
-- existing `UsePathSeg` (validation.fenel:67-83). The parent ADT already
-- carries `RsnQuantifiedReflection {channel, path}` — the brief's named
-- reason. This module adds ZERO reason constructors.
--
-- SLICE-3b POSTURE: INERT. Nothing here is judgment-reachable. No checker,
-- decider, kernel, or dispatch path consumes it; no summary exists, so every
-- Fenel-bodied call fences. 3b lands the domain, the table, the gate, the
-- summary SCHEMA and the profile scope; 3c wires the typed integration and 3d
-- the simultaneous recursive summaries.
--
-- SLICE-3d ADDITION: THE TYPED OBSERVATION PROVENANCE BOUNDARY. 3b's public
-- entry took its parameter provenance as an ARGUMENT, so `obs.shell.complete`
-- was a CONTRACT ON THE CALLER rather than an enforced invariant. 3d moves
-- origination INSIDE the judgment: `vobAnalyze` now takes ONE frozen
-- `ObsRequest` carrying the body, the DECLARED parameter types, and the
-- quantifier vector, and derives every parameter's provenance itself through
-- the closed `ObsRepr` descriptor. No caller-controlled parameter seed reaches
-- it. The pre-originated entry survives as `vobAnalyzeFromProvenance`, marked
-- ANALYSIS-INTERNAL, so the ~90-case algebra battery can still drive shell and
-- opaque scrutinees directly; it carries NO judgment authority and the phase-4
-- static gate is what keeps it unreachable from production.
--
-- WHAT ORIGINATION IS ALLOWED TO CONCLUDE, and why it is deliberately blunt.
-- A declared type is NOT a representation proof (finding 2, below), so
-- `vobDeriveRepr` never witnesses a shell: it answers GROUND or OPAQUE only.
-- It is opaque over every ordinal the declared type mentions, and over EVERY
-- ordinal in scope when the type carries a `$el` node — because that is how the
-- compatibility encoding spells a higher-kinded application `f a`, whose head
-- `f` is a bare STRING there and whose quantified identity lives in the
-- authoritative `TypeScheme.applications` sidecar (`types.ts`'s
-- `SchemeApplicationBase`) that this traversal does not consult. A `$var` scan
-- alone would answer GROUND for `f Number` — a live false admission, since
-- instantiating `f` as `List` versus `Maybe` changes the runtime shape.
--
-- "NO FENCE" IS POSITIVE TRUSTED CONTENT once 3c consumes it — it authorizes
-- `Validated`. So the classifier's EXHAUSTIVENESS is a TCB claim, carried as
-- ledger rows in the same commit, not an abstention that "adds nothing".
--
-- THE FOUND-BIT SIDE CONDITION (rewritten by signature-substrate slice 3c-D1).
-- The prior text here argued the REBUTTED position -- that no Fenel-typed value
-- can be host-`undefined`, so `{var: x}` cannot observe a found bit. Round 2 of
-- the 3b review disproved that with a registered counterexample, which is why
-- the row went MISSING. Slice 3c does not re-establish it: `resolveVar` now
-- threads an explicit FOUND BIT, so ABSENT and PRESENT-holding-`undefined` no
-- longer collapse and only ABSENCE reaches the registry projection / fallback.
-- The read is therefore not an observation even if an invalid host value leaks
-- in. Row `obs.var.undefined` is SIDE-CONDITIONED on evaluator surfaces
-- (enumerable own data; every strategy presents its scope as own data), not on
-- native honesty. See design/tcb-ledger.md for the conditions.
--
-- FUNCTION PREFIX: every function here carries the `vob` family prefix so the
-- phase-4 static gate can prove non-reachability by scanning ONE namespace
-- (the `vlg` ledger / `vrg` rigid precedent).
-- =========================================================================

-- ---- 3b-D1 — the abstract domain (SHAPE PROVENANCE, not a Boolean) --------

-- One payload slot of a shell: the key a projection or pattern reads it at,
-- and that payload's own provenance.
@entity
@label "ObsProvSlot"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — one payload slot of a shape-provenance shell: the key a projection or pattern reads it at, and that payload's provenance."
ObsProvSlot = ObsProvSlot key: String prov: ObsProv

-- The abstract domain. A BINARY taint lattice loses the distinction that
-- decides admissibility: matching the fixed `Maybe` shell of a `Maybe κ` is
-- not the same act as observing an arbitrary `a`. So the domain is shape
-- provenance.
--
--  * `PvClean`  — the whole value is instantiation-INDEPENDENT.
--  * `PvShell`  — the outer former is `shape` and EVERY observation of that
--                 former (its `$tag`, its key set, its extent) is
--                 instantiation-independent; the payload reachable at key `k`
--                 has provenance `slots[k]`. `Maybe κ` is
--                 `PvShell "Maybe" [ObsProvSlot "_0" (PvOpaque [0])]`: a
--                 `$tag: "Just"` discrimination is ADMISSIBLE (the shell is
--                 fixed at every instantiation — the tag varies with the
--                 VALUE, which is not what equivariance is about), while
--                 projecting `_0` yields the opaque payload and any
--                 observation of THAT fences.
--  * `PvOpaque` — the value's representation IS a rigid's. `rigids` is the SET
--                 of contributing quantifier ORDINALS (3a's alpha-normal
--                 identity), which buys correct `∀a b.` call-instantiation
--                 mapping, honest diagnostics naming the binder, and the
--                 future selective relaxations. It is cheap: ordinals only.
@entity
@label "ObsProv"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the shape-provenance abstract domain. PvClean = instantiation-independent; PvShell = outer former fixed with per-slot payload provenance (what distinguishes matching a Maybe shell from observing an arbitrary `a`); PvOpaque = the representation IS a rigid's, carrying the contributing quantifier ordinals."
ObsProv =
  PvClean
  | PvShell shape: String slots: [ObsProvSlot]
  | PvOpaque rigids: [Nat]

-- The sequence carrier: a positional argument/element list's provenances plus
-- the reasons accumulated while walking it. Internal.
@entity
@label "ObsProvList"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the internal sequence carrier: a positional list of provenances plus the reasons accumulated walking it."
ObsProvList = ObsProvList provs: [ObsProv] reasons: [ValidationReason]

-- The walker's result at one node: the provenance of the value that node
-- EVALUATES TO, plus every reason accumulated so far. Reasons accumulate; the
-- analysis reports ALL of them, never just the first.
@entity
@label "ObsState"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the walker result at one node: the provenance of the value the node evaluates to, plus every accumulated reason (all of them, never just the first)."
ObsState = ObsState prov: ObsProv reasons: [ValidationReason]

-- One lexical binding in scope, at its provenance.
@entity
@label "ObsBind"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — one lexical binding in scope at its shape provenance."
ObsBind = ObsBind name: String prov: ObsProv

-- The result of classifying ONE pattern against a scrutinee's provenance.
@entity
@label "ObsPatOutcome"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the result of classifying one raw pattern against a scrutinee's provenance: admissibility, the binders it introduces at their provenances, and the reasons it raised."
ObsPatOutcome = ObsPatOutcome admissible: Boolean binds: [ObsBind] reasons: [ValidationReason]

-- The scope-threading carrier for the BINDING forms. `let` bindings, `where`
-- bindings and a `do` sequence's inline `{let: …}` items all extend the scope
-- their SIBLINGS see, so those folds must return the extended scope alongside
-- the value and the reasons — a reasons-only fold would silently drop a `do`
-- item's binders before the next statement reads them.
@entity
@label "ObsScopeState"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the scope-threading carrier for the binding forms: the value's provenance, the accumulated reasons, AND the extended scope, because let/where bindings and a do sequence's inline let items all extend the scope their siblings see."
ObsScopeState = ObsScopeState prov: ObsProv reasons: [ValidationReason] binds: [ObsBind]

-- ---- 3b-D2 — the raw-form transfer table (as DATA) -----------------------

-- The transfer class of one raw evaluator form. Two observer strengths, and
-- the split is load-bearing:
--
--  * `VfcShapeObserver` observes the OUTER former only (`length` reads extent;
--    a `$tag` test reads the discriminator; a key-presence test reads the key
--    set). Admissible on `PvClean` AND on `PvShell` — the shell asserts the
--    outer former is instantiation-independent. Fences on `PvOpaque`.
--  * `VfcObserver` reads INTO the payload (`deepEq` recurses; `in` compares
--    elements; `toNumber`/`String` coerce). Admissible only when the argument
--    is GROUND — no `PvOpaque` anywhere inside it.
--
-- Collapsing the two into one strength would either fence `length` of a
-- literal array (needless) or admit `deepEq` over a `Maybe κ` (unsound).
--
-- `VfcEnvPath` is the THIRD, and it is not a refinement of the other two: its
-- form's arguments are raw PATH NAMES that the runtime resolves in the DATA
-- CONTEXT, so the observation is of the ENVIRONMENT, not of an argument. A
-- transfer table keyed on argument provenance cannot express it — the reason the
-- table is an exhaustiveness obligation and the WALKER is the authority.
@entity
@label "ObsFormClass"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the transfer class of one raw evaluator form. VfcShapeObserver reads the outer former only (admissible on a shell); VfcObserver reads into the payload (admissible only on a ground argument); VfcFence always fences; VfcUnreachable cannot occur in a stored raw body."
ObsFormClass =
  VfcLiteral
  | VfcPassthrough note: String
  | VfcStructural note: String
  | VfcShapeObserver channel: String
  | VfcObserver channel: String
  | VfcEnvPath channel: String
  | VfcCall note: String
  | VfcFence detail: String
  | VfcUnreachable detail: String

-- One row of the transfer table. `form` is the RAW spelling: a `KNOWN_OPS`
-- key verbatim, or a `«…»`-bracketed pseudo-form naming one of `evaluate`'s
-- non-op dispatch tiers (the brackets cannot collide with any op key, since a
-- JSON-Logic op key is an identifier or an operator notation).
@entity
@label "ObsFormRule"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — one row of the raw-form transfer table: the raw form spelling (a KNOWN_OPS key verbatim, or a «…»-bracketed pseudo-form naming one of evaluate's non-op dispatch tiers) and its transfer class."
ObsFormRule = ObsFormRule form: String class: ObsFormClass

-- ---- 3b-D4 — the proof-summary schema (schema only, unpopulated) ---------

-- A callee summary is NOT a Boolean "passed D2". It is an INPUT→OUTPUT
-- PROVENANCE RELATION tied to an exact scheme and an exact ACTIVE
-- implementation, plus its invalidation key.
--
-- `outputDerivesFrom` lists the parameter indices whose taint reaches the
-- result. `outputIntrinsicRigids` is the separate fact that the result TYPE
-- itself mentions a quantified variable — that taints the output with NO
-- tainted actual, which is exactly what a return-position typeclass operation
-- (`default : a`, unified-dispatch.md:157) does.
--
-- RECURSION IS NOT HANDLED BY ORDINARY CALLEE CLOSURE. A recursive or mutually
-- recursive function has no already-proved callee summary, so a transitive
-- rule that assumes one REJECTS recursion and is no foundation for later
-- accepting it. Such functions need a SIMULTANEOUS SCC proof, or a monotone
-- fixed point over provisional summaries. **Slice 3d owns that.** This slice
-- ships the schema and leaves it unpopulated: every Fenel-bodied call fences.
@entity
@label "ObsProvSummary"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the callee proof-summary SCHEMA (unpopulated in this slice): an input→output provenance relation tied to an exact scheme and an exact active implementation, plus its invalidation key. outputDerivesFrom = the param indices whose taint reaches the result; outputIntrinsicRigids = the result type itself mentions a quantified variable (return-position taint with no tainted actual). Recursive callees need a simultaneous SCC proof — slice 3d."
ObsProvSummary = ObsProvSummary targetId: String schemeHash: String origin: String profile: String version: String paramCount: Nat formals: [String] observesFrom: [Nat] outputDerivesFrom: [Nat] outputIntrinsicRigids: Boolean invalidationKey: String

-- ---- 3b-D3 — the frozen call-target record -------------------------------

-- Everything the call gate is allowed to know about one call, RESOLVED and
-- FROZEN by the caller. The validator may not reconstruct any of it.
--
--  * `sourceTargetId` / `flatTargetId` — the declaring module's frozen source
--    frame answer and the FLAT runtime (`ctx.getFunction`) answer. The ledger
--    records the counterexample where they differ (validation-ledger.fenel:44-58):
--    a code-name collision on the key-as-fnId form resolves locally in the
--    source frame and flat-globally at runtime. Both answers are positive and
--    they DISAGREE, so evidence may not be minted from either — gate rule 1.
--  * `origin` — the ACTIVE implementation branch, not "has a body". Verified
--    order in `invokeFunction` (json-logic.ts:2370-2412): `nativesCtx[spec.id]`
--    → `nativesCtx[name]` → `natives[spec.id]` → `natives[name]` → `spec.body`.
--    A ctx-native WINS over a Fenel body, so body presence is not safety.
--    Vocabulary is the `ImplementationOrigin` tag set the ledger already
--    admits (`vlgKnownOrigin`) plus two this analysis needs: `FenelBody`, and
--    `BuiltinOpNative` for the branch `ImplementationOrigin` does not model
--    (json-logic.ts:2348-2351 — reachable only when a name has NO registration
--    and no native, so it is not an origin of any registration).
--  * NOTE: there is deliberately NO `supplied` slot. How many arguments a call
--    supplies is a property of the call SITE, not of the callee: one frozen
--    record describes a target that two sites may apply differently. The walker
--    already knows the count and passes it, so a stale or optimistic `supplied`
--    in a frozen record cannot weaken the arity or dispatch-position rules.
--  * `dispatchRoute` — `RDirect` | `RDispatch` | `RReturnPosition` | `RUnknown`.
--    Only a SATURATED, IN-RANGE `RDispatch` reaches `rsvTypeKey`
--    (dispatch.fenel:333-360: `pos < 0` ⇒ NoInstance, `pos ≥ |args|` ⇒
--    UnderApplied), so the return-position and under-applied cases are
--    separate route values rather than a negative ordinal.
--  * `resultRigids` — the CALLER-side ordinals the instantiated result type
--    mentions. Exact rather than a Boolean, so `∀a b.` output taint maps to the
--    right binder; and it is the channel by which a return-position typeclass
--    operation taints its result with NO tainted actual at all.
--  * `profile` — the execution profile this record was frozen for (3b-D5).
@entity
@label "ObsCallTarget"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the frozen call-target record the gate consumes: the raw key, the frozen source-frame AND flat-runtime targets (a disagreement fences), the ACTIVE implementation branch (a ctx-native wins over a Fenel body, so body presence is not safety), the dispatch route and position, the declared arity, the caller-side ordinals the instantiated result type mentions, the execution profile, the dependency identity, and the callee summary (always Nothing in this slice). Deliberately carries NO argument count — how many arguments a call supplies is a property of the call SITE, so the walker passes it and a stale record cannot weaken the arity rule."
ObsCallTarget = ObsCallTarget rawKey: String sourceTargetId: String flatTargetId: String origin: String tier: String key: String dispatchRoute: String dispatchPos: Nat arity: Nat resultRigids: [Nat] profile: String dependencyId: String summary: Maybe ObsProvSummary

-- The analysis outcome. `ObsFenced` accumulates reasons rather than stopping at
-- the first (the census needs the multiset, and a first-reason-only report would
-- make rule ablation impossible); `ObsAdmitted` carries the body's result
-- provenance and the profile set the verdict is ABOUT.
--
-- "EVERY reason" IS TOO STRONG, and 3d's round-2 review was right to say so.
-- Two call-gate rules RETURN EARLY -- a frozen source-frame-versus-flat target
-- disagreement, and a target belonging to an uncovered profile -- so a record
-- that trips either is never put through the well-formedness, arity, ambient,
-- dispatch or branch rules, and its reason list is genuinely partial. That is
-- fail-CLOSED (the form fences either way), so it costs diagnostics rather than
-- soundness; the accurate statement is "accumulates, and never stops at the
-- first merely because it found one".
@entity
@label "ObsOutcome"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the observation-fence outcome: ObsFenced ACCUMULATING reasons rather than stopping at the first (rule ablation needs the multiset; two call-gate rules do return early, so a fenced record's list is not guaranteed exhaustive — fail-closed, so it costs diagnostics rather than soundness), or ObsAdmitted with the body's result provenance and the profile set the verdict covers."
ObsOutcome =
  ObsFenced reasons: [ValidationReason]
  | ObsAdmitted prov: ObsProv profiles: [String]

-- ---- 3d-D1 — the ORIGINATION domain (the typed provenance boundary) ------

-- One quantifier of the checked scheme. `sourceName` is the spelling the
-- compatibility type body uses in a `{$var: …}` node; `id` is the GENERATED
-- identity (`q0`, `q1`, …) that the authoritative application sidecar keys on.
-- The two namespaces are kept SEPARATE and are never tried against one
-- another: `collide : a -> q0 -> a` is legal source, and matching a `$var`
-- against either slot would resolve `{$var: "q0"}` to the FIRST quantifier by
-- generated id when it denotes the SECOND by source name. The census helper
-- this replaces did exactly that.
--
-- The ORDINAL of a quantifier is its INDEX in the scheme's vector — 3a's
-- alpha-normal identity — never a slot of this record.
@entity
@label "ObsQuantifier"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — one quantifier of the checked scheme: the GENERATED identity (q0, q1, … — what the authoritative application sidecar keys on) and the SOURCE spelling (what a compatibility {$var} node uses). The two namespaces are never tried against one another: `collide : a -> q0 -> a` is legal source, so matching a $var against either slot would resolve it to the wrong binder. A quantifier's ORDINAL is its index in the vector, never a field here."
ObsQuantifier = ObsQuantifier id: String sourceName: String

-- One payload slot of a representation descriptor.
@entity
@label "ObsReprSlot"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — one payload slot of a representation descriptor: the key a projection or pattern reads it at, and that payload's own descriptor."
ObsReprSlot = ObsReprSlot key: String repr: ObsRepr

-- The CLOSED representation descriptor. 3b's `vobOriginateParam` took an OPEN
-- record, so "the descriptor" was whatever a caller chose to hand in; this is
-- the closed ADT the ledger's `obs.origin.descriptor` row always described.
--
--  * `RprGround`     — no quantified variable can reach this value's
--                      representation. Yields `PvClean`.
--  * `RprOpaque`     — the representation MAY DEPEND ON these ordinals. Stated
--                      as a sound SUPERSET, not as "the representation IS a
--                      rigid's": origination over-approximates on purpose and
--                      an over-large set only ever fences more.
--  * `RprTransparent`— an ERASED wrapper: the value's representation is its
--                      INNER's, so the descriptor INHERITS the inner one
--                      recursively. 3b's row claimed this and the code returned
--                      the opaque atom because no inner was supplied; 3d-D2
--                      supplies it.
--  * `RprShell`      — a POSITIVELY WITNESSED runtime former, whose slots must
--                      carry the payload's COMPLETE taint (`obs.shell.complete`).
--
-- HONESTY: `vobDeriveRepr` — the only in-tree producer, and the only one the
-- public entry can reach — emits `RprGround` or `RprOpaque` and NOTHING ELSE.
-- `RprTransparent` and `RprShell` are ATTESTATIONS this ADT cannot verify: a
-- closed constructor is not a witness. They exist because the fence must have a
-- place to put a real per-profile representation witness when one is produced,
-- and because D2 requires the transparent contract to be IMPLEMENTED rather
-- than merely described. Reachable today only from the analysis-internal entry.
@entity
@label "ObsRepr"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the CLOSED representation descriptor a parameter's provenance is originated from (3b took an open record). RprGround = no quantified variable reaches the representation; RprOpaque = the representation MAY depend on these ordinals (a sound superset, not an identity); RprTransparent = an erased wrapper that INHERITS its inner descriptor recursively; RprShell = a positively witnessed runtime former whose slots must carry the payload's complete taint. The only in-tree producer emits Ground or Opaque only — Transparent and Shell are attestations a closed constructor cannot witness."
ObsRepr =
  RprGround
  | RprOpaque ordinals: [Nat]
  | RprTransparent inner: ObsRepr
  | RprShell shape: String slots: [ObsReprSlot]

-- One declared parameter of the checked function: the binder spelling the body
-- reads it at, and its DECLARED TYPE as a marshalled carrier. The type is the
-- input, not a provenance — that is the whole point of the boundary.
@entity
@label "ObsParam"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — one declared parameter of the checked function: the binder spelling its body reads it at, and its DECLARED TYPE as a marshalled carrier. The type is the input and the provenance is DERIVED from it; a caller cannot supply a provenance."
ObsParam = ObsParam name: String declared: (JsonLogic Any)

-- The FROZEN analysis request — one record, not a parallel-list argument
-- vector, so a parameter and its declared type cannot drift apart in transit,
-- and the identity fields give the CONSUMER something to bind the verdict to.
--
-- IT IS NOT A CORRESPONDENCE CHECK, and an earlier draft of this comment said
-- it was. Nothing here compares the parameter list against the registered
-- function's own parameters or against the scheme: a caller that omits a
-- parameter, or describes a genuinely quantified one with a ground declared
-- type, gets exactly what it asked for. The record removes the PARALLEL-LIST
-- misalignment hazard; establishing that the parameters ARE the registration's
-- is the authenticated producer's obligation.
--
-- WHAT THE IDENTITY FIELDS ARE AND ARE NOT. `bodyHash` / `schemeHash` /
-- `validatorVersion` / `registryProfile` are carried, checked for
-- NON-EMPTINESS, and reported — they are the invalidation identity a consumer
-- must re-establish against the registration it is about to trust. This module
-- does NOT recompute them from the body it was handed, so they bind the
-- verdict, they do not authenticate the request. Saying otherwise would be the
-- over-claim the register exists to prevent.
--
-- `lowering` and `evaluator` are SEPARATE AXES and neither is the registry
-- profile. Interpreted-versus-compiled is a lowering question; Eager / Lazy /
-- Partial / Jit / an explicit `evaluateWith` is an evaluator-ENTRY question;
-- SYSTEM-versus-seed is a registry question. 3b's single `profile` string
-- conflated them, which is why `obs.gate.ambient` could read as a claim about
-- the whole engine when it was a claim about `invokeFunction`.
@entity
@label "ObsRequest"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the FROZEN analysis request: the raw body, the declared parameters, the quantifier vector, the frozen call targets, the profile scope, and the invalidation identity (body hash, scheme hash, registry profile, validator version). Lowering and evaluator entry are SEPARATE axes from the registry profile — 3b's single profile string conflated all three. The identity fields BIND the verdict for a consumer to re-establish; this module does not recompute them, so they do not authenticate the request."
ObsRequest = ObsRequest callerId: String body: (JsonLogic Any) params: [ObsParam] quantified: [ObsQuantifier] targets: [ObsCallTarget] bodyHash: String schemeHash: String validatorVersion: String registryProfile: String lowering: String evaluator: String analysedProfiles: [String] requiredProfiles: [String]

-- =========================================================================
-- carrier constructors
--
-- Every carrier is built through a one-line constructor rather than an inline
-- record literal. That is not cosmetic: the Fenel grammar continues STATEMENTS
-- across lines but not EXPRESSIONS, so a record literal spanning lines inside a
-- `then`/`else` branch or a `let` value terminates the enclosing form early
-- (`Unexpected else`). Routing every construction through these keeps the
-- walker's branch arms single-expression by construction.
-- =========================================================================

@label "observe: stateOf"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — build a walker state from a provenance and the accumulated reasons. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobStateOf : (p: ObsProv) -> (rs: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobStateOf p rs = ObsState { prov = p, reasons = rs }

@label "observe: provListOf"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — build a sequence carrier from a positional provenance list and the accumulated reasons. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobProvListOf : (ps: List ObsProv) -> (rs: List ValidationReason) -> ObsProvList
vobProvListOf ps rs = ObsProvList { provs = ps, reasons = rs }

@label "observe: scopeOf"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — build a scope-threading carrier from a provenance, the accumulated reasons, and the extended scope. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobScopeOf : (p: ObsProv) -> (rs: List ValidationReason) -> (bs: List ObsBind) -> ObsScopeState
vobScopeOf p rs bs = ObsScopeState { prov = p, reasons = rs, binds = bs }

@label "observe: patOf"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — build a pattern-classification outcome from admissibility, the binders introduced, and the accumulated reasons. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobPatOf : (ok: Boolean) -> (bs: List ObsBind) -> (rs: List ValidationReason) -> ObsPatOutcome
vobPatOf ok bs rs = ObsPatOutcome { admissible = ok, binds = bs, reasons = rs }

@label "observe: slotOf"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — build one payload slot from a key and its provenance. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobSlotOf : (k: String) -> (p: ObsProv) -> ObsProvSlot
vobSlotOf k p = ObsProvSlot { key = k, prov = p }

@label "observe: shellOf"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — build a shell provenance from a shape and its payload slots. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobShellOf : (shape: String) -> (slots: List ObsProvSlot) -> ObsProv
vobShellOf shape slots = PvShell { shape = shape, slots = slots }

-- NORMALIZING: an EMPTY ordinal set yields `PvClean`, which makes an opaque
-- atom over no ordinals UNCONSTRUCTIBLE. That is load-bearing, not tidiness.
-- `vobIsGround` reads emptiness as ground, so an opaque atom over an empty set
-- would be simultaneously "opaque" (fencing shape observers) and "ground"
-- (admitting deep observers) — an inconsistent value the join could otherwise
-- manufacture from `PvOpaque [] ⊔ PvClean`. Routing every construction through
-- here removes the case instead of asking every consumer to remember it.
-- (Adopted from the 3b design review's join caveat.)
@label "observe: opaqueOf"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — build an opaque provenance over a quantifier-ordinal set, NORMALIZING an empty set to PvClean so an opaque atom over no ordinals is unconstructible. Load-bearing: vobIsGround reads emptiness as ground, so such an atom would fence shape observers while admitting deep observers — an inconsistent value the join could otherwise manufacture."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobOpaqueOf : (rs: List Nat) -> ObsProv
vobOpaqueOf rs = if eq (length rs) 0 then PvClean else PvOpaque { rigids = rs }

-- =========================================================================
-- the ordinal set algebra
-- =========================================================================

@label "observe: hasOrdinal"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — is this quantifier ordinal already in the set? Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobHasOrdinal : (rs: List Nat) -> (o: Nat) -> Boolean
vobHasOrdinal rs o = case head rs of
  Nothing -> false
  Just r -> if eq r o then true else vobHasOrdinal (eufRest rs) o

@label "observe: addOrdinal"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — add one quantifier ordinal to a set (idempotent). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobAddOrdinal : (rs: List Nat) -> (o: Nat) -> List Nat
vobAddOrdinal rs o = if vobHasOrdinal rs o then rs else appendItem o rs

@label "observe: unionOrdinals"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — set union of two quantifier-ordinal sets. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobUnionOrdinals : (left: List Nat) -> (right: List Nat) -> List Nat
vobUnionOrdinals left right = case head right of
  Nothing -> left
  Just o -> vobUnionOrdinals (vobAddOrdinal left o) (eufRest right)

-- =========================================================================
-- the provenance lattice
-- =========================================================================

-- Every ordinal contributing anywhere inside a provenance — the outer atom AND
-- every payload slot, recursively.
@label "observe: rigidsOf"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — every quantifier ordinal contributing anywhere inside a provenance: the outer atom and every payload slot, recursively."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobRigidsOf : (p: ObsProv) -> List Nat
vobRigidsOf p = case p of
  PvClean -> []
  PvOpaque { rigids = rs } -> rs
  PvShell { slots = sl } -> vobRigidsOfSlots sl []

@label "observe: rigidsOfSlots"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — vobRigidsOf accumulated over a shell's payload slots. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobRigidsOfSlots : (sl: List ObsProvSlot) -> (acc: List Nat) -> List Nat
vobRigidsOfSlots sl acc = case head sl of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just s -> vobRigidsOfSlots (eufRest sl) (vobUnionOrdinals acc (vobRigidsOf s.prov))

-- GROUND = no rigid anywhere inside. This is the admissibility test for a DEEP
-- observer, and it is strictly stronger than "the outer former is fixed".
@label "observe: isGround"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — is this provenance rigid-free at every depth? The admissibility test for a DEEP observer (one that reads into the payload), strictly stronger than 'the outer former is fixed'. An opaque atom answers false UNCONDITIONALLY, including one carrying an empty ordinal set: vobOpaqueOf normalizes that away, but the ADT is PUBLIC, so a malformed atom is constructible from outside the module's own producers — and it would otherwise read as ground and admit every deep observation. Slice 3d removed the parameter-seed channel from the public entry; the ADT stays public, so this arm stays unconditional."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobIsGround : (p: ObsProv) -> Boolean
vobIsGround p = case p of
  PvOpaque -> false
  _ -> eq (length (vobRigidsOf p)) 0

-- OUTER-SHAPE FIXED = the value's own former is instantiation-independent.
-- True for `PvClean` (nothing about it varies) and for every `PvShell` (that
-- is exactly the shell's assertion); false for `PvOpaque`.
@label "observe: shapeFixed"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — is the value's OUTER former instantiation-independent? True for PvClean and for every PvShell (the shell's own assertion); false for PvOpaque. The admissibility test for a shape observer."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobShapeFixed : (p: ObsProv) -> Boolean
vobShapeFixed p = case p of
  PvOpaque -> false
  _ -> true

-- Collapse a provenance to its taint content, forgetting the shape: `PvClean`
-- when nothing is tainted, otherwise the opaque atom over every contributing
-- ordinal. Used wherever a shape claim can no longer be sustained.
@label "observe: taint"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — collapse a provenance to its taint content, forgetting the shape: PvClean when rigid-free, otherwise the opaque atom over every contributing ordinal. Used wherever a shape claim can no longer be sustained."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobTaint : (p: ObsProv) -> ObsProv
vobTaint p = vobOpaqueOf (vobRigidsOf p)

@label "observe: slotLookup"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the provenance of a shell's payload at one key, if the slot is modelled. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobSlotLookup : (sl: List ObsProvSlot) -> (k: String) -> Maybe ObsProv
vobSlotLookup sl k = case head sl of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just s -> if eq s.key k then Just s.prov else vobSlotLookup (eufRest sl) k

-- The JOIN (least upper bound). The one deliberate imprecision is
-- `PvClean ⊔ PvShell = vobTaint PvShell`: `PvClean` carries NO shape, so the
-- join cannot verify that the two sides agree on the outer former, and
-- claiming a shell whose shape may not hold would be unsound. Sound (it only
-- ever adds taint) and it degrades `if c then Nothing else Just x` from a
-- `Maybe` shell to an opaque atom. Over-fencing is safe; over-resolving is
-- not. The refinement is a future `PvGround shape` case that records a
-- literal's former; it is NOT a bug to be "fixed" by weakening the join.
@label "observe: join"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the provenance join (least upper bound). Same-shape shells join slotwise; differing shapes collapse to the opaque union. PvClean joined with a shell collapses to the shell's taint, because PvClean carries no shape and the join cannot verify the formers agree — sound, deliberately imprecise, documented."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobJoin : (a: ObsProv) -> (b: ObsProv) -> ObsProv
vobJoin a b = case a of
  PvClean -> case b of
    PvClean -> PvClean
    _ -> vobTaint b
  PvOpaque { rigids = ra } -> vobOpaqueOf (vobUnionOrdinals ra (vobRigidsOf b))
  PvShell { shape = sa, slots = la } -> case b of
    PvClean -> vobTaint a
    PvOpaque { rigids = rb } -> vobOpaqueOf (vobUnionOrdinals (vobRigidsOf a) rb)
    PvShell { shape = sb, slots = lb } ->
      if eq sa sb
      then vobShellOf sa (vobJoinSlots la lb)
      else vobOpaqueOf (vobUnionOrdinals (vobRigidsOf a) (vobRigidsOf b))

-- Slotwise join over the UNION of the two key sets. A key present on only one
-- side keeps that side's provenance: it means the other branch's value lacks
-- the key entirely, so a pattern requiring it simply fails on that branch and
-- observes no rigid there.
@label "observe: joinSlots"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — slotwise join over the UNION of two shells' key sets. A key present on only one side keeps that side's provenance (the other branch's value lacks it, so a pattern requiring it fails there and observes nothing). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobJoinSlots : (la: List ObsProvSlot) -> (lb: List ObsProvSlot) -> List ObsProvSlot
vobJoinSlots la lb = vobJoinSlotsRight (vobJoinSlotsLeft la lb []) la lb

@label "observe: joinSlotsLeft"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the left half of the slotwise join: every key of la, joined with lb's slot at that key when present. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobJoinSlotsLeft : (la: List ObsProvSlot) -> (lb: List ObsProvSlot) -> (acc: List ObsProvSlot) -> List ObsProvSlot
vobJoinSlotsLeft la lb acc = case head la of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just s ->
    let joined = case vobSlotLookup lb s.key of
          Nothing -> s.prov
          Just other -> vobJoin s.prov other
    vobJoinSlotsLeft (eufRest la) lb (appendItem (ObsProvSlot { key = s.key, prov = joined }) acc)

@label "observe: joinSlotsRight"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the right half of the slotwise join: append lb's slots whose key la does not carry. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobJoinSlotsRight : (acc: List ObsProvSlot) -> (la: List ObsProvSlot) -> (lb: List ObsProvSlot) -> List ObsProvSlot
vobJoinSlotsRight acc la lb = case head lb of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just s ->
    let next = case vobSlotLookup la s.key of
          Nothing -> appendItem s acc
          Just _ -> acc
    vobJoinSlotsRight next la (eufRest lb)

-- The join over a branch list. An EMPTY list is `PvClean`: a form with no
-- branches evaluates to host-null, which is instantiation-independent.
@label "observe: joinList"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the provenance join over a branch list. An empty list is PvClean: a form with no branches evaluates to host-null, which is instantiation-independent."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobJoinList : (ps: List ObsProv) -> ObsProv
vobJoinList ps = case head ps of
  Nothing -> PvClean
  Just p -> vobJoinListFrom (eufRest ps) p

@label "observe: joinListFrom"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — fold vobJoin over a branch list from a seed. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobJoinListFrom : (ps: List ObsProv) -> (acc: ObsProv) -> ObsProv
vobJoinListFrom ps acc = case head ps of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just p -> vobJoinListFrom (eufRest ps) (vobJoin acc p)

-- =========================================================================
-- reason constructors (existing ValidationReason cases only)
-- =========================================================================

@label "observe: reflection reason"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the RsnQuantifiedReflection row for an observation of a κ-typed value, naming the channel and the typed path. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobReflect : (channel: String) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> ValidationReason
vobReflect channel path = RsnQuantifiedReflection { channel = channel, path = path }

@label "observe: unsupported-form reason"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the RsnUnsupportedSyntax row for a raw form this analysis declines to model. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobUnsupported : (form: String) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> ValidationReason
vobUnsupported form path = RsnUnsupportedSyntax { form = form, path = path }

@label "observe: abstain reason"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the RsnCheckerAbstained row for a deliberate abstention that is not itself a reflection. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobAbstain : (detail: String) -> ValidationReason
vobAbstain detail = RsnCheckerAbstained { detail = detail }

-- =========================================================================
-- 3b-D2 — the transfer table
-- =========================================================================

-- The COMPLETE raw evaluator form set: NINE non-op dispatch tiers as `«…»`
-- pseudo-forms plus all forty `KNOWN_OPS` verbatim. The exhaustiveness
-- meta-test re-derives BOTH halves from `json-logic.ts` and asserts a two-way
-- match: no evaluator-dispatchable form without a row (which would let a form
-- inherit a default), and no row without a form (which would let a stale row
-- claim coverage it does not have).
--
-- THE ARITHMETIC, stated exactly, because 3b's prose here said "twelve tiers"
-- beside a NINE-entry list and the ledger said nine. `evaluate` has TWELVE
-- return arms. ONE is the `KNOWN_OPS` arm, which expands into the forty ops.
-- The other ELEVEN group into these NINE tier classes: `«dollar-marker»` covers
-- BOTH the single-key and the multi-key `$`-prefixed arms, and `«record»` covers
-- BOTH the single-field and the non-single-key record-literal arms (the latter
-- also handles the ZERO-key object). Slice 3d re-derives the ARM inventory from
-- source so neither the grouping nor the count can drift silently
-- (`obs.form.arms`); the arm-to-class ASSIGNMENT stays a human-audited
-- correspondence, which is why that row is an AXIOM and not a theorem.
--
-- The thirty-two `BUILTIN_OP_NATIVES` keys are deliberately NOT rows: they are
-- reachable ONLY through tier `«key-as-fnId»`, whose row routes them to the
-- call gate. The meta-test pins that separately by classifying each of them.
-- `evaluate`'s NON-OP dispatch tiers, as `«…»`-bracketed pseudo-forms. The
-- brackets cannot collide with a real op key: a JSON-Logic op key is an
-- identifier or an operator notation, and the parser emits neither bracket.
--
-- UNIT PARAMETER, and it is not decoration: a bare lowercase identifier with no
-- lexical binding resolves through `resolveVar`'s registry fall-through to a
-- `{$ref: id}` VALUE rather than being CALLED (json-logic.ts:1613-1622). A
-- nullary enumeration referenced by name would therefore hand every consumer a
-- reference instead of a list — `head` of which is `Nothing`, so
-- `vobIsKnownOp` would silently answer FALSE for every op and route all forty
-- through the key-as-fnId path. The unit parameter forces a real application.
@label "observe: tier names"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — evaluate's NON-OP dispatch tiers as «…»-bracketed pseudo-forms. The brackets cannot collide with a real op key (a JSON-Logic op key is an identifier or an operator notation; the parser emits neither bracket)."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobTierNames : (unit: Any) -> List String
vobTierNames unit =
  [ "«null»", "«scalar»", "«array»", "«closure»", "«bytes»", "«tagged»"
  , "«dollar-marker»", "«record»", "«key-as-fnId»"
  ]

-- All forty `KNOWN_OPS`, verbatim. Membership in THIS list is what separates a
-- structural op from a key-as-fnId call head, so it is kept apart from the tier
-- pseudo-forms rather than folded in.
@label "observe: op names"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3e - all forty KNOWN_OPS, READ FROM the shared decomposition roster rather than kept as a second copy. Membership is what separates a structural op from a key-as-fnId call head, so it stays apart from the tier pseudo-forms."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobOpNames : (unit: Any) -> List String
vobOpNames unit = fdcOpNames unit

@label "observe: form names"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the COMPLETE raw evaluator form set: evaluate's non-op dispatch tiers plus all forty KNOWN_OPS. The exhaustiveness meta-test asserts a two-way match against json-logic.ts, so neither a missing row nor a stale row can pass."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobFormNames : (unit: Any) -> List String
vobFormNames unit = concat (vobTierNames unit) (vobOpNames unit)

-- The classifier. TOTAL over strings: an unrecognized form answers
-- `VfcFence`, so a forty-first op added to the evaluator fences here rather
-- than inheriting an existing form's semantics. That default is the whole
-- reason the enumeration above is checked in both directions.
@label "observe: classify form"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the raw-form transfer classifier. Total over strings: an unrecognized form answers VfcFence, so a new evaluator op fences rather than inheriting an existing form's semantics."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobClassifyForm : (form: String) -> ObsFormClass
vobClassifyForm form =
  if eq form "«null»" then VfcLiteral
  else if eq form "«scalar»" then VfcLiteral
  else if eq form "«array»" then VfcStructural { note = "array literal: elementwise, extent fixed" }
  else if eq form "«closure»" then VfcUnreachable { detail = "a JS closure value cannot occur in a stored raw body" }
  else if eq form "«bytes»" then VfcUnreachable { detail = "an ArrayBuffer view cannot occur in a stored raw body" }
  else if eq form "«tagged»" then VfcPassthrough { note = "self-evaluating: returned untouched, so wholly literal" }
  else if eq form "«dollar-marker»" then VfcPassthrough { note = "inert data marker: returned untouched" }
  else if eq form "«record»" then VfcStructural { note = "record literal: fields evaluated at their keys" }
  else if eq form "«key-as-fnId»" then VfcCall { note = "the universal call form; also the sole route to BUILTIN_OP_NATIVES" }
  else if eq form "var" then VfcStructural { note = "binder read; a DOTTED path is a payload projection" }
  else if eq form "missing" then VfcEnvPath { channel = "missing" }
  else if eq form "missing_some" then VfcEnvPath { channel = "missing_some" }
  else if eq form "if" then VfcStructural { note = "lazy; each condition is a truthy TEST" }
  else if eq form "?:" then VfcStructural { note = "lazy; each condition is a truthy TEST" }
  else if eq form "match" then VfcStructural { note = "structural matching; see the M1-M6 pattern rules" }
  else if eq form "and" then VfcStructural { note = "lazy; every operand is truthy-TESTED and the operand VALUE is returned" }
  else if eq form "or" then VfcStructural { note = "lazy; every operand is truthy-TESTED and the operand VALUE is returned" }
  else if eq form "min" then VfcObserver { channel = "min" }
  else if eq form "max" then VfcObserver { channel = "max" }
  else if eq form "&" then VfcObserver { channel = "bitand" }
  else if eq form "|" then VfcObserver { channel = "bitor" }
  else if eq form "^" then VfcObserver { channel = "bitxor" }
  else if eq form "~" then VfcObserver { channel = "bitnot" }
  else if eq form "<<" then VfcObserver { channel = "shiftleft" }
  else if eq form ">>" then VfcObserver { channel = "shiftright" }
  else if eq form "substr" then VfcObserver { channel = "substr" }
  else if eq form "length" then VfcShapeObserver { channel = "length" }
  else if eq form "in" then VfcObserver { channel = "in" }
  else if eq form "merge" then VfcObserver { channel = "merge" }
  else if eq form "map" then VfcFence { detail = "raw-rule intrinsic: the rule runs in a DERIVED per-item data context this analysis cannot see" }
  else if eq form "filter" then VfcFence { detail = "raw-rule intrinsic: the rule runs in a DERIVED per-item data context this analysis cannot see" }
  else if eq form "reduce" then VfcFence { detail = "raw-rule intrinsic: the rule runs in a DERIVED per-item data context this analysis cannot see" }
  else if eq form "all" then VfcFence { detail = "raw-rule intrinsic: the rule runs in a DERIVED per-item data context this analysis cannot see" }
  else if eq form "some" then VfcFence { detail = "raw-rule intrinsic: the rule runs in a DERIVED per-item data context this analysis cannot see" }
  else if eq form "none" then VfcFence { detail = "raw-rule intrinsic: the rule runs in a DERIVED per-item data context this analysis cannot see" }
  else if eq form "let" then VfcStructural { note = "sequential bindings; the LAST binding's value is the result" }
  else if eq form "do" then VfcStructural { note = "statement sequence; inline let items bind into the enclosing scope" }
  else if eq form "ann" then VfcStructural { note = "annotation stripped; only argument 0 is evaluated" }
  else if eq form "where" then VfcStructural { note = "local bindings then the body" }
  else if eq form "withInstance" then VfcFence { detail = "binds a block-scoped instance, changing dispatch resolution inside its extent" }
  else if eq form "type_def" then VfcFence { detail = "registers dynamic constructor names, changing how LATER construct and pattern forms resolve" }
  else if eq form "construct" then VfcStructural { note = "the primary shell producer: outer former fixed, payload slots per argument" }
  else if eq form "method" then VfcCall { note = "qualified dispatch: the dispatch argument is REFLECTED" }
  else if eq form "deepEq" then VfcObserver { channel = "deepEq" }
  else if eq form "call" then VfcCall { note = "explicit application; the `$` head is dynamic" }
  else if eq form "pipe" then VfcFence { detail = "dynamic application: the callee identity is not statically an exact target" }
  else if eq form "|>" then VfcFence { detail = "dynamic application: the callee identity is not statically an exact target" }
  else if eq form "fn" then VfcStructural { note = "lambda: captures the enclosing scope; parameters bind opaquely" }
  else if eq form "apply" then VfcFence { detail = "dynamic application: the callee identity is not statically an exact target" }
  else VfcFence { detail = "raw form absent from the transfer table" }

-- The table, projected from the enumeration through the classifier so the two
-- can never drift.
@label "observe: form table"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the raw-form transfer table as DATA, projected from the form enumeration through the classifier so the two cannot drift."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobFormTable : (unit: Any) -> List ObsFormRule
vobFormTable unit = map (\f -> ObsFormRule { form = f, class = vobClassifyForm f }) (vobFormNames unit)

-- =========================================================================
-- the scope
-- =========================================================================

@label "observe: bind lookup"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the provenance of a lexical binding, if bound. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobBindLookup : (bs: List ObsBind) -> (n: String) -> Maybe ObsProv
vobBindLookup bs n = case head bs of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just b -> if eq b.name n then Just b.prov else vobBindLookup (eufRest bs) n

-- Innermost-first shadowing: a new binding is PREPENDED so it wins the lookup
-- above, exactly as a `let` rebinding of an existing name shadows it in the
-- runtime's copied data context.
@label "observe: bind with"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — extend a scope with one binding, PREPENDED so it shadows an existing same-named binder (matching the runtime's copied data context). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobBindWith : (bs: List ObsBind) -> (n: String) -> (p: ObsProv) -> List ObsBind
vobBindWith bs n p = concat [ObsBind { name = n, prov = p }] bs

-- 3d-D4 — WINNER-FIRST, and the direction is the whole rule.
--
-- `vobBindLookup` takes the FIRST match, so the HEAD of a scope list is its
-- winner. `add` therefore arrives ALREADY winner-first and is CONCATENATED,
-- not folded through the prepending `vobBindWith`.
--
-- The 3b implementation folded, which REVERSES `add`. Two same-spelling
-- binders in one pattern then resolved to the runtime's LOSER, by a DOUBLE
-- reversal: `vobPatternStructural` accumulates field by field through this
-- function (giving a correct winner-first list on its own), and `vobMatchArms`
-- then installs that list through this function AGAIN, putting the earlier
-- field back in front. The runtime's answer is the opposite: `matchPattern`
-- walks the pattern's keys in order and writes each binder with
-- `defineDataContextBinding`, whose descriptor is `configurable: true,
-- writable: true` (json-logic.ts:34-41), so a LATER key OVERWRITES an earlier
-- one and the LAST occurrence in a successful depth-first key walk wins.
--
-- Concatenation is correct at EVERY nesting depth, which a single-site repair
-- would not have been: the structural and array pattern folds call this too, so
-- with the fold the winner alternated with depth. (The 3b review's finding on
-- this named only the installation site; fixing only that site would have left
-- nested patterns wrong in the other direction.)
@label "observe: bind all"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — extend a scope with a WINNER-FIRST list of bindings by CONCATENATION. vobBindLookup takes the first match, so add's head is its winner and must stay in front. 3b folded through the prepending vobBindWith, which reverses add — and since the structural, array and arm-installation sites all call this, two same-spelling binders resolved to the runtime's LOSER by a double reversal. The runtime's winner is the LAST occurrence in a successful depth-first pattern-key walk, because defineDataContextBinding redefines a configurable, writable property (json-logic.ts:34-41)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobBindAll : (bs: List ObsBind) -> (add: List ObsBind) -> List ObsBind
vobBindAll bs add = concat add bs

@label "observe: env with"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — a copy of the analysis environment carrying an extended lexical scope. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobEnvWith : (env: a) -> (binds: List ObsBind) -> a
vobEnvWith env binds =
  { callerId = env.callerId, targets = env.targets, ordinals = env.ordinals, binds = binds, profiles = env.profiles }

-- =========================================================================
-- the observation primitives
-- =========================================================================

-- A DEEP observation of one argument: admissible only when the argument is
-- rigid-free at every depth.
@label "observe: deep observation"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — record a DEEP observation of one value (an observer that reads into the payload). Admissible only when the value is rigid-free at every depth; otherwise a RsnQuantifiedReflection row naming the channel."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobObserveDeep : (channel: String) -> (p: ObsProv) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobObserveDeep channel p path acc =
  if vobIsGround p then acc else appendItem (vobReflect channel path) acc

-- An OUTER-SHAPE observation of one argument: admissible on `PvClean` and on
-- every `PvShell`, since a shell asserts its own former is
-- instantiation-independent. Fences on `PvOpaque`.
@label "observe: shape observation"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — record an OUTER-SHAPE observation of one value (extent, discriminator, key set). Admissible on PvClean and on every PvShell (a shell asserts its former is instantiation-independent); fences on PvOpaque."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobObserveShape : (channel: String) -> (p: ObsProv) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobObserveShape channel p path acc =
  if vobShapeFixed p then acc else appendItem (vobReflect channel path) acc

-- A deep observation over a whole positional list.
@label "observe: deep observation over a list"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — vobObserveDeep over every provenance in a positional list. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobObserveDeepAll : (channel: String) -> (ps: List ObsProv) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobObserveDeepAll channel ps path acc = case head ps of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just p -> vobObserveDeepAll channel (eufRest ps) path (vobObserveDeep channel p path acc)

-- =========================================================================
-- payload projection
-- =========================================================================

-- Project one key off a value. `resolveVar` reads DOTTED paths straight off a
-- bound value (json-logic.ts:1587-1603), so `{var: "bot.token"}` is a
-- projection, not a plain lexical occurrence.
--
--  * `PvClean`  — every part of a clean value is clean.
--  * `PvOpaque` — projecting a field off a value whose representation IS a
--                 rigid's observes that representation. FENCE, and propagate
--                 the taint so no downstream rule mistakes the result for
--                 clean.
--  * `PvShell`  — the modelled slot FIRST, then `length` as the extent (an
--                 outer-shape observation), then an abstention. **The order is
--                 load-bearing**: a record can carry an OWN `length` field, and
--                 both `matchPattern` and `resolveVar` read it verbatim, so
--                 answering "clean extent" before consulting the slots would
--                 hand back a clean provenance for a payload that may be
--                 κ-typed (the round-2 review's counterexample). An UNMODELLED
--                 key abstains rather than defaulting, because it means the
--                 slot model is incomplete for that former.
@label "observe: project"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — project one key off a value, mirroring resolveVar's dotted-path read. A clean value projects clean; an opaque value FENCES (projecting a field off a rigid-represented value observes that representation) and propagates its taint; a shell yields the modelled slot, treats `length` as an extent observation, and ABSTAINS on an unmodelled key rather than defaulting."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobProject : (p: ObsProv) -> (k: String) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobProject p k path acc = case p of
  PvClean -> vobStateOf (PvClean) (acc)
  PvOpaque -> vobStateOf (p) (appendItem (vobReflect "var-projection" path) acc)
  PvShell { slots = sl } -> case vobSlotLookup sl k of
    Just child -> vobStateOf child acc
    Nothing ->
      if eq k "length"
      then vobStateOf PvClean (vobObserveShape "length" p path acc)
      else vobStateOf (vobTaint p) (appendItem (vobAbstain "projection of an unmodelled shell slot") acc)

-- A DOTTED variable read projects off a bound value's payload
-- (json-logic.ts:1587-1603 splits the path and reads field by field). The
-- binder ROOT is recovered by prefix, exactly as the ledger's
-- `vlgHasBinderPath` does, so no string split is needed:
--
--  * a clean root projects CLEAN — nothing about a clean value varies, at any
--    depth, so reading a field of one is not an observation;
--  * an OPAQUE root FENCES: projecting a field off a value whose representation
--    IS a rigid's observes that representation;
--  * a SHELL root ABSTAINS: the exact slot needs the path tail, which this
--    slice does not split. 3c's typed sidecar resolves it. The result carries
--    the shell's whole taint so nothing downstream mistakes it for clean.
@label "observe: project dotted"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the provenance of a DOTTED variable read off a binder root. A clean root projects clean; an opaque root FENCES (projecting a field off a rigid-represented value observes that representation); a shell root ABSTAINS with its whole taint, because resolving the exact slot needs the path tail that 3c's typed sidecar supplies."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobProjectDotted : (p: ObsProv) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobProjectDotted p path acc = case p of
  PvClean -> vobStateOf (PvClean) (acc)
  PvOpaque -> vobStateOf (p) (appendItem (vobReflect "var-projection" path) acc)
  PvShell -> vobStateOf (vobTaint p) (appendItem (vobAbstain "dotted projection into a shell payload") acc)

-- =========================================================================
-- small structural helpers (mirrored, never borrowed — a `vlg*` call from this
-- module would break the ledger's own single-namespace static gate)
-- =========================================================================

@label "observe: nameIn"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — is a spelling present in a string list? Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobNameIn : (names: List String) -> (n: String) -> Boolean
vobNameIn names n = case head names of
  Nothing -> false
  Just x -> if eq x n then true else vobNameIn (eufRest names) n

-- Terminates on an EXHAUSTED SLICE, not on `length`: `length` counts Unicode
-- code POINTS while `slice` indexes UTF-16 code UNITS, so a length bound stops
-- early on any astral character and MISSES a dot past it — which would silently
-- turn a data-dependent projection back into a plain binder read. (The ledger
-- recorded this exact defect at `vlgDotFrom`.)
@label "observe: dot scan"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — scan a spelling for a dot separator, terminating on an exhausted slice rather than a code-point length (slice indexes UTF-16 units while length counts code points, so a length bound misses a dot past an astral character). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobDotFrom : (name: String) -> (index: Nat) -> Boolean
vobDotFrom name index =
  let ch = slice name index (add index 1)
  if eq ch ""
  then false
  else if eq ch "."
  then true
  else vobDotFrom name (add index 1)

@label "observe: isDotted"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — does this spelling carry a dot field-projection separator? Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobIsDotted : (name: String) -> Boolean
vobIsDotted name = vobDotFrom name 0

-- The binder a spelling reads FROM: the exact binder, or the binder that is a
-- proper dotted prefix of it (`b` is the root of `b.f`). Binder spellings are
-- identifiers and cannot themselves contain a dot, so at most one root matches
-- and there is no longest-prefix ambiguity.
@label "observe: root binder"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the lexical binder a spelling reads from: the exact binder, or the binder that is a proper dotted prefix of it (b is the root of b.f). Binder spellings cannot contain a dot, so at most one root matches. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobRootBinder : (bs: List ObsBind) -> (name: String) -> Maybe ObsBind
vobRootBinder bs name = case head bs of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just b ->
    if eq b.name name
    then Just b
    else if startsWith name (concat b.name ".")
    then Just b
    else vobRootBinder (eufRest bs) name

@label "observe: tailList"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the list without its head (the empty list when absent). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobTailList : (items: a) -> a
vobTailList items = case tail items of
  Nothing -> []
  Just rest -> rest

@label "observe: dropTwo"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the list without its first two elements (an if/match pair, or the method form's class and method names). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobDropTwo : (items: a) -> a
vobDropTwo items = vobTailList (vobTailList items)

@label "observe: lastItem"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the final element of a JsonLogic item list, treating an empty tail remainder as the end (tail of a singleton is Just of the empty list, not Nothing). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobLastItem : (items: a) -> Maybe (JsonLogic Any)
vobLastItem items = case head items of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just first -> case tail items of
    Nothing -> Just first
    Just rest -> if eq (length rest) 0 then Just first else vobLastItem rest

@label "observe: nth prov"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the provenance at one position of a positional list. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobNthProv : (ps: List ObsProv) -> (index: Nat) -> Maybe ObsProv
vobNthProv ps index = case head ps of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just p -> if eq index 0 then Just p else vobNthProv (eufRest ps) (sub index 1)

-- The positional payload key for one constructor argument. Rendered from a
-- FIXED table rather than by converting the ordinal to a string: a cloned
-- decider context BOXES host numbers, so `toString` on one yields the
-- host object rendering (the recorded landmine). An arity past the table
-- yields an unmodelled slot, which ABSTAINS — the honest answer.
@label "observe: positional key"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the positional payload key _0, _1, … for one constructor argument, from a FIXED table rather than by number-to-string conversion (a cloned decider context boxes host numbers, so toString yields the host object rendering). An arity past the table yields an unmodelled slot, which abstains. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobPositionalKey : (i: Nat) -> String
vobPositionalKey i =
  if eq i 0 then "_0"
  else if eq i 1 then "_1"
  else if eq i 2 then "_2"
  else if eq i 3 then "_3"
  else if eq i 4 then "_4"
  else if eq i 5 then "_5"
  else if eq i 6 then "_6"
  else if eq i 7 then "_7"
  else if eq i 8 then "_8"
  else if eq i 9 then "_9"
  else if eq i 10 then "_10"
  else if eq i 11 then "_11"
  else "«positional-overflow»"

-- The conservatively-unknown provenance for THIS check scope. With NO
-- quantified ordinals in scope nothing can be κ-typed, so `PvClean` is exact
-- rather than optimistic — and `PvOpaque []` would be WRONG here, because an
-- empty ordinal set reads as GROUND (`vobRigidsOf` is empty) and would silently
-- admit every observation.
@label "observe: unknown prov"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the conservatively-unknown provenance for a check scope: opaque over every ordinal in scope, or PvClean when the scope quantifies nothing (with no ordinals nothing can be κ-typed). Never an opaque atom over an EMPTY ordinal set — that reads as GROUND and would admit every observation."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobUnknownProv : (ordinals: List Nat) -> ObsProv
vobUnknownProv ordinals = vobOpaqueOf ordinals

@label "observe: capture prov"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the provenance of a lambda's CAPTURED environment: the join over every binding in scope, since fnOp copies the whole data context (json-logic.ts:2556). This is what makes handing a taint-capturing closure to a native fence. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobCaptureProv : (bs: List ObsBind) -> ObsProv
vobCaptureProv bs = vobCaptureFrom bs PvClean

@label "observe: capture from"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — fold the join over a scope's binding provenances. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobCaptureFrom : (bs: List ObsBind) -> (acc: ObsProv) -> ObsProv
vobCaptureFrom bs acc = case head bs of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just b -> vobCaptureFrom (eufRest bs) (vobJoin acc (vobTaint b.prov))

@label "observe: bind params"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — bind a list of parameter spellings to one provenance. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobBindParams : (bs: List ObsBind) -> (names: List String) -> (p: ObsProv) -> List ObsBind
vobBindParams bs names p = case head names of
  Nothing -> bs
  Just n -> vobBindParams (vobBindWith bs n p) (eufRest names) p

@label "observe: target lookup"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the frozen call-target record for one raw key, if the caller froze one. A missing record is an unresolved use, never an assumption. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobTargetLookup : (ts: List ObsCallTarget) -> (rawKey: String) -> Maybe ObsCallTarget
vobTargetLookup ts rawKey = case head ts of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just t -> if eq t.rawKey rawKey then Just t else vobTargetLookup (eufRest ts) rawKey

-- =========================================================================
-- 3b-D3 — the active-origin call gate (strict v1)
-- =========================================================================

-- The ACTIVE non-Fenel implementation branches. `HostNative` /
-- `NativeWithFallback` / `ExternalHandler` are the `ImplementationOrigin` tags
-- the sibling inventory already admits (`vlgKnownOrigin`); `BuiltinOpNative` is
-- the FIFTH branch `ImplementationOrigin` does not model
-- (json-logic.ts:2348-2351), reachable only for a raw key with NO registration
-- and no native — so it is not an origin OF a registration, but it IS an active
-- host implementation and must gate like one.
@label "observe: host-active branch"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — is this the ACTIVE non-Fenel implementation branch? HostNative / NativeWithFallback / ExternalHandler are the ImplementationOrigin tags, plus BuiltinOpNative — the fifth branch ImplementationOrigin does not model (json-logic.ts:2348-2351), reachable only for a raw key with no registration and no native, yet still an active host implementation."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobBranchIsHostActive : (origin: String) -> Boolean
-- There is deliberately NO companion `isKnownOrigin` predicate. The closed set
-- of admitted origins is encoded ONCE, by `vobBranchGate`'s cascade: host-active
-- here, `FenelBody` next, everything else an unresolved use. A second predicate
-- listing the same tags is a drift risk with no consumer.
vobBranchIsHostActive origin =
  if eq origin "HostNative" then true
  else if eq origin "NativeWithFallback" then true
  else if eq origin "ExternalHandler" then true
  else if eq origin "BuiltinOpNative" then true
  else false

-- GATE RULE 2 — the DEEPEST channel. Only a SATURATED, IN-RANGE `RDispatch`
-- route reaches `rsvTypeKey` (dispatch.fenel:333-360: a negative position is
-- `NoInstance`, a position at or past the argument count is `UnderApplied`).
-- When it does, the resolved INSTANCE — i.e. WHICH CODE RUNS — is selected from
-- the runtime type of the dispatch argument, so a non-ground argument there
-- makes target selection instantiation-dependent. That is not a wrapper detail;
-- it is the whole execution.
@label "observe: dispatch reflection gate"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — gate rule 2, the deepest channel: an in-range RDispatch route reflects its dispatch argument to select the instance, so a non-ground argument there makes WHICH CODE RUNS instantiation-dependent. Keyed on the SITE argument count, not on declared arity. An under-applied dispatch eta-defers into a closure that re-dispatches later, and a return-position route resolves no instance at all; both abstain."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobDispatchGate : (t: ObsCallTarget) -> (argProvs: List ObsProv) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobDispatchGate t argProvs path acc =
  if eq t.dispatchRoute "RDispatch"
  then
    if lt t.dispatchPos (length argProvs)
    then case vobNthProv argProvs t.dispatchPos of
      Nothing -> appendItem (vobAbstain "dispatch position past the analysed argument list") acc
      Just p -> if vobIsGround p then acc else appendItem (vobReflect "dispatch-argument" path) acc
    else appendItem (vobAbstain "under-applied dispatch eta-defers into a closure that re-dispatches on arguments this analysis never sees") acc
  else if eq t.dispatchRoute "RReturnPosition"
  then appendItem (vobAbstain "return-position dispatch resolves no instance from any argument") acc
  else if eq t.dispatchRoute "RDirect"
  then acc
  else appendItem (vobAbstain "unrecognized dispatch route") acc

-- GATE RULES 3-5 — the ACTIVE implementation branch, not "has a body".
--
--  * A host-active branch receiving a NON-GROUND argument fences. The criterion
--    is the BRANCH, never a hand-written list of reflective callees: an
--    exception list is exactly the enumerate-and-guard posture the S0 gate
--    withdrew.
--    NOTE (a deliberate, documented widening of the brief's wording): the brief
--    says "a non-`Clean` argument". The implemented criterion is NON-GROUND,
--    which is strictly weaker and still sound — if no rigid occurs ANYWHERE in
--    a value then substituting κ := τ does not change that value at all, so the
--    native's result is identical at every instantiation. It is also NECESSARY:
--    a literal array is `PvShell "«array»"`, ground but not `PvClean`, and
--    fencing it would fence `length [1,2,3]`. Soundness rests on the invariant
--    that EVERY shell this module constructs carries its complete taint in its
--    slots (array literal: the element join; record literal: every field;
--    construct: both readings of the payload; closure: the whole capture;
--    tagged: wholly literal). A future shell producer that models only SOME
--    payload would break `vobIsGround` on a shell and must not be added.
--  * A Fenel-bodied callee is modularly admissible ONLY against a summary. This
--    slice ships the schema unpopulated, so every such call fences with
--    MissingEvidence. The interface is built and tested; 3c and 3d turn it on.
--  * An unrecognized origin is an unresolved use.
@label "observe: branch gate"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — gate rules 3 to 5: a host-active branch receiving a NON-GROUND argument fences (the criterion is the active BRANCH, never a hand-written list of reflective callees); a Fenel-bodied callee is admissible only against a provenance summary, which this slice never has; an unrecognized origin is an unresolved use."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobBranchGate : (t: ObsCallTarget) -> (argProvs: List ObsProv) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobBranchGate t argProvs path acc =
  if vobBranchIsHostActive t.origin
  then vobObserveDeepAll (concat "host-implementation:" t.origin) argProvs path acc
  else if eq t.origin "FenelBody"
  then case t.summary of
    Nothing -> appendItem (RsnMissingEvidence { useId = t.rawKey, observed = "no provenance summary: slice 3b ships the schema unpopulated and 3d owns the simultaneous recursive proof" }) acc
    Just s -> vobSummaryGate t s argProvs path acc
  else appendItem (RsnUnresolvedSignatureUse { useId = t.rawKey, status = concat "unrecognized active implementation origin: " t.origin }) acc

-- A summary authorizes a call only when it is a summary OF THIS CALL: the same
-- target, the same ACTIVE implementation, and the same execution profile. A
-- summary proved against an interpreted body does not cover the compiled
-- lowering, and one proved before a native was installed does not cover the
-- registration afterwards.
@label "observe: summary gate"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — a provenance summary authorizes a call only when it is a summary OF THIS CALL: same target, same ACTIVE implementation, same execution profile. A summary proved against an interpreted body does not cover the compiled lowering, and one proved before a native was installed does not cover the registration afterwards."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobSummaryGate : (t: ObsCallTarget) -> (s: ObsProvSummary) -> (argProvs: List ObsProv) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobSummaryGate t s argProvs path acc =
  if not (eq s.targetId t.sourceTargetId)
  then appendItem (RsnStaleEvidence { useId = t.rawKey, observed = "summary target does not match the frozen call target" }) acc
  else if not (eq s.origin t.origin)
  then appendItem (RsnStaleEvidence { useId = t.rawKey, observed = "summary implementation origin does not match the active branch" }) acc
  else if not (eq s.profile t.profile)
  then appendItem (RsnStaleEvidence { useId = t.rawKey, observed = "summary execution profile does not match the frozen profile" }) acc
  else if not (eq s.paramCount t.arity)
  then appendItem (RsnStaleEvidence { useId = t.rawKey, observed = "summary parameter count does not match the frozen target arity" }) acc
  else if not (eq (length s.formals) t.arity)
  then appendItem (RsnStaleEvidence { useId = t.rawKey, observed = "summary formal vector does not match the frozen target arity" }) acc
  else if not (eq s.invalidationKey t.dependencyId)
  then appendItem (RsnStaleEvidence { useId = t.rawKey, observed = "summary invalidation key does not match the frozen dependency identity" }) acc
  else if eq s.schemeHash ""
  then appendItem (RsnStaleEvidence { useId = t.rawKey, observed = "summary carries no scheme hash" }) acc
  else if eq s.version ""
  then appendItem (RsnStaleEvidence { useId = t.rawKey, observed = "summary carries no producer version" }) acc
  else vobObservedInputGate s argProvs path acc

-- OUTPUT TAINT. The result of a call is tainted when EITHER the instantiated
-- result type mentions a caller rigid — which happens with NO tainted actual at
-- all, exactly what a return-position typeclass operation does — OR the callee's
-- summary says the output derives from a tainted input.
--
-- `resultRigids` is the caller-side instantiation and is authoritative here;
-- the summary's `outputIntrinsicRigids` is the callee-side fact that its own
-- scheme puts a quantified variable in the result, recorded separately because
-- the two are established by different parties.
@label "observe: call output"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the provenance of a call's RESULT: tainted when the instantiated result type mentions a caller rigid (which happens with NO tainted actual — a return-position typeclass operation) or when the callee summary says the output derives from a tainted input."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobCallOutput : (t: ObsCallTarget) -> (argProvs: List ObsProv) -> ObsProv
vobCallOutput t argProvs =
  let fromInputs = case t.summary of
        Nothing -> []
        Just s -> vobSummaryInputTaint s argProvs []
  vobOpaqueOf (vobUnionOrdinals t.resultRigids fromInputs)

@label "observe: summary input taint"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the ordinals a summary's declared input-to-output derivation carries from the actual arguments. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobSummaryInputTaint : (s: ObsProvSummary) -> (argProvs: List ObsProv) -> (acc: List Nat) -> List Nat
vobSummaryInputTaint s argProvs acc = vobTaintFromIndices s.outputDerivesFrom argProvs acc

@label "observe: taint from indices"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the union of the argument provenances' ordinals at a list of parameter indices. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobTaintFromIndices : (idxs: List Nat) -> (argProvs: List ObsProv) -> (acc: List Nat) -> List Nat
vobTaintFromIndices idxs argProvs acc = case head idxs of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just i ->
    let next = case vobNthProv argProvs i of
          Nothing -> vobAllArgOrdinals argProvs acc
          Just p -> vobUnionOrdinals acc (vobRigidsOf p)
    vobTaintFromIndices (eufRest idxs) argProvs next

@label "observe: all arg ordinals"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — every ordinal contributing anywhere in an argument list. Used when a summary names an output-derivation index the analysed argument list does not have: the conservative answer is the whole argument taint, never nothing. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobAllArgOrdinals : (ps: List ObsProv) -> (acc: List Nat) -> List Nat
vobAllArgOrdinals ps acc = case head ps of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just p -> vobAllArgOrdinals (eufRest ps) (vobUnionOrdinals acc (vobRigidsOf p))

-- GATE RULE 1 first, then 2, then 3-5, then the output.
--
-- Rule 1 closes the seam the ledger recorded (validation-ledger.fenel:44-58):
-- the declaring module's FROZEN source frame and the FLAT runtime resolution can
-- both answer positively and DISAGREE, on a code-name collision reached through
-- the key-as-fnId form. Evidence may not be minted from either answer, so a
-- disagreement fences before any other rule runs.
@label "observe: gate target"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the call gate over one frozen target: rule 1 fences a source-frame-versus-flat-runtime target disagreement (the ledger's recorded P4-D0a seam, where both answers are positive and differ), then the profile check, the dispatch-argument reflection rule, the active-branch rules, and finally the result provenance."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobGateTarget : (t: ObsCallTarget) -> (argProvs: List ObsProv) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: a) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobGateTarget t argProvs path env acc =
  if not (eq t.sourceTargetId t.flatTargetId)
  then vobStateOf (vobJoinList argProvs) (appendItem (RsnUnresolvedSignatureUse { useId = t.rawKey, status = "frozen source-frame and flat-runtime targets disagree" }) acc)
  else if not (vobNameIn env.profiles t.profile)
  then vobStateOf (vobJoinList argProvs) (appendItem (vobAbstain "frozen call target belongs to an execution profile this verdict does not cover") acc)
  else
    let afterWellFormed = vobTargetIssues t env.ordinals acc
    let afterArity = vobArityGate t (length argProvs) path afterWellFormed
    let afterNamed = vobAmbientGate t env.ordinals path afterArity
    let afterDispatch = vobDispatchGate t argProvs path afterNamed
    let afterBranch = vobBranchGate t argProvs path afterDispatch
    vobStateOf (vobCallOutput t argProvs) (afterBranch)

@label "observe: gate call"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — resolve a raw call key to its frozen call-target record and run the gate. A key with NO frozen record is an unresolved use, never an assumption."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobGateCall : (rawKey: String) -> (argProvs: List ObsProv) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: a) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobGateCall rawKey argProvs path env acc =
  case vobTargetLookup env.targets rawKey of
    Nothing -> vobStateOf (vobUnknownProv env.ordinals) (appendItem (RsnUnresolvedSignatureUse { useId = rawKey, status = "no frozen call-target record" }) acc)
    Just t -> vobGateTarget t argProvs path env acc

-- =========================================================================
-- 3b-D2 — the node walk (the transfer table, applied)
-- =========================================================================

-- vobWalk — the shape cascade, mirroring `evaluate` (json-triple-logic.ts:1198-1277)
-- tier for tier. Every arm returns the provenance of the value the node
-- EVALUATES TO, not of the node itself.
--
--  * scalars and host-null are wholly literal;
--  * an ARRAY LITERAL is a shell whose extent is fixed, carrying the JOIN of its
--    elements at one `«element»` slot. Element-indexed slots are deliberately
--    not modelled: that would need an ordinal-to-string rendering, and the join
--    is the sound answer for every index;
--  * a `$tag` value is SELF-EVALUATING (returned untouched), so it is wholly
--    literal — its nested `{var: …}`-shaped fields are never evaluated;
--  * a `$`-keyed object at either arity is an inert data marker, likewise
--    returned untouched and therefore literal;
--  * a RECORD LITERAL is a shell over its evaluated fields, keyed by field name.
--
-- The two `evaluate` tiers a stored body cannot reach — a live JS closure value
-- and an `ArrayBuffer` view — have no arm because the marshalled `JsonLogic`
-- carrier has no case for them; they are `VfcUnreachable` rows in the table so
-- the exhaustiveness meta-test still accounts for them.
@label "observe: walk"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the node walk, mirroring evaluate's dispatch tiers. Scalars are literal; an array literal is a fixed-extent shell carrying the JOIN of its elements; a $tag value and a $-keyed marker are returned untouched and so wholly literal; a record literal is a shell over its evaluated fields. Every arm returns the provenance of the value the node EVALUATES TO."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobWalk : (node: (JsonLogic Any)) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: a) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobWalk node path env acc = case fdcNodePlan node of
  FdcPlanInert -> vobStateOf (PvClean) (acc)
  FdcPlanSeq { items = xs } ->
    let seq = vobWalkSeq xs path 0 env acc []
    vobStateOf (vobShellOf "«array»" [vobSlotOf "«element»" (vobJoinList seq.provs)]) seq.reasons
  FdcPlanRecord { fields = fs } ->
    if eq (length fs) 0
    then vobStateOf (PvClean) (acc)
    else vobWalkRecord fs path env acc []
  FdcPlanOp { op = op, rawArgs = raw, argList = args, schedule = sched } -> vobFormOp op raw args sched path env acc
  FdcPlanKeyed { op = op, rawArgs = raw, argList = args, unresolved = fb } -> vobKeyAsFnId op args path env acc

@label "observe: walk sequence"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — walk a positional item list at VpsSeq, collecting each item's provenance in order. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobWalkSeq : (items: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (index: Nat) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> (provs: List ObsProv) -> ObsProvList
vobWalkSeq items path index env acc provs = case head items of
  Nothing -> vobProvListOf (provs) (acc)
  Just item ->
    let st = vobWalk item (appendItem (VpsSeq { index = index }) path) env acc
    vobWalkSeq (eufRest items) path (add index 1) env st.reasons (appendItem st.prov provs)

@label "observe: walk args"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — walk a positional argument list at VpsArg, collecting each argument's provenance in order. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobWalkArgs : (items: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (index: Nat) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> (provs: List ObsProv) -> ObsProvList
vobWalkArgs items path index env acc provs = case head items of
  Nothing -> vobProvListOf (provs) (acc)
  Just item ->
    let st = vobWalk item (appendItem (VpsArg { index = index }) path) env acc
    vobWalkArgs (eufRest items) path (add index 1) env st.reasons (appendItem st.prov provs)

@label "observe: walk record"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — walk a record literal's fields at VpsField into a shell keyed by field name. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobWalkRecord : (fields: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> (slots: List ObsProvSlot) -> ObsState
vobWalkRecord fields path env acc slots = case head fields of
  Nothing -> vobStateOf (PvShell { shape = "«record»", slots = slots }) (acc)
  Just f ->
    let st = vobWalk f.value (appendItem (VpsField { key = f.name }) path) env acc
    vobWalkRecord (eufRest fields) path env st.reasons (appendItem (ObsProvSlot { key = f.name, prov = st.prov }) slots)

-- vobSingleKey — the single-key dispatcher. The structural forms that need
-- scope or laziness get named arms; EVERY remaining known op is dispatched
-- THROUGH the transfer table, so the table is load-bearing rather than
-- decorative, and an unrecognized key falls to the key-as-fnId call form
-- (which the runtime decides by RESOLUTION, not value shape).
@label "observe: walk slots"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3e - walk exactly the argument slots the runtime EVALUATES, at their raw index, collecting each provenance in order. The eager intrinsics do not all consume every slot: the bitwise binaries read two, ~ and length one, in two, substr two plus an optional third, and deepEq / withInstance evaluate NOTHING at any arity but two. Observing the residue charged observations against children the runtime never reaches. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobWalkSlots : (slots: [FdcCallSlot]) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: a) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> (provs: List ObsProv) -> ObsProvList
vobWalkSlots slots path env acc provs = case head slots of
  Nothing -> vobProvListOf (provs) (acc)
  Just s ->
    if not s.evaluated
    then vobWalkSlots (eufRest slots) path env acc provs
    else
      let st = vobWalk s.node (appendItem (VpsArg { index = s.rawIndex }) path) env acc
      vobWalkSlots (eufRest slots) path env st.reasons (appendItem st.prov provs)

-- vobFormOp — SLICE 3e. The single-key cascade this replaces was a second
-- copy of the evaluator's own form classification; it now dispatches on the
-- SHARED closed `FdcForm`, so a form cannot be structural here and a call
-- there. What stays vob-owned is the SEMANTIC half: which observation each
-- form performs. That mapping is the transfer table, and it is deliberately
-- not shared — `vlg*` treats the same runtime operations as binder-only.
@label "observe: form op"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3e - dispatch one KNOWN_OP on the SHARED closed form classification. The structural half (which form, which child slots) comes from the shared decomposition; the semantic half (which observation each form performs) stays in this analysis's transfer table."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobFormOp : (op: String) -> (rawArgs: (JsonLogic Any)) -> (argList: a) -> (sched: FdcSchedule) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobFormOp op rawArgs argList sched path env acc =
  case sched.form of
    FdcFormVar -> vobVarUse argList path env acc
    FdcFormEnvPath { kind = k } -> vobEnvPathOp k argList path env acc
    FdcFormLazy -> vobLazyForm op argList path env acc
    FdcFormBinding { kind = k } -> vobBindingForm k argList path env acc
    FdcFormMatch -> vobMatchOp argList path env acc
    FdcFormAnn -> vobAnnOp argList path env acc
    FdcFormLambda -> vobFnOp argList path env acc
    FdcFormConstruct -> vobConstructOp argList path env acc
    FdcFormCall -> vobCallOp argList path env acc
    FdcFormMethod -> vobMethodOp argList path env acc
    FdcFormTypeDef -> vobStateOf PvClean (appendItem (vobAbstain "type_def registers dynamic constructor names, changing how LATER construct and pattern forms resolve — a state change this analysis does not model") acc)
    _ -> vobTabledOp op (fdcScheduledSlots sched.slots argList) path env acc

@label "observe: lazy form"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3e - the short-circuit structural ops. The conditional and the boolean operators differ in what they RETURN (a branch versus the operand value), so they keep separate transfers. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobLazyForm : (op: String) -> (argList: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobLazyForm op argList path env acc =
  if eq op "and"
  then vobBoolOp "and-operand" argList path env acc
  else if eq op "or"
  then vobBoolOp "or-operand" argList path env acc
  else vobIfOp argList path env acc

@label "observe: binding form"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3e - dispatch the three sequentially-scoped binding forms. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobBindingForm : (kind: String) -> (argList: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobBindingForm kind argList path env acc =
  if eq kind "let"
  then vobLetOp argList path env acc
  else if eq kind "do"
  then vobDoOp argList path env acc
  else vobWhereOp argList path env acc

-- The residual known ops, dispatched by their table class. A known op reaching
-- here with a class that is not an observer or a fence is a TABLE/WALKER
-- disagreement, so it abstains loudly rather than defaulting to a call.
@label "observe: tabled op"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — dispatch a residual KNOWN_OP by its transfer-table class: a shape observer reads the outer former only, a deep observer requires ground arguments, a fence always fences. A known op whose class is neither is a table-versus-walker disagreement and abstains loudly rather than defaulting to a call."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobTabledOp : (op: String) -> (slots: [FdcCallSlot]) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobTabledOp op slots path env acc =
  let seq = vobWalkSlots slots path env acc []
  case vobClassifyForm op of
    VfcShapeObserver { channel = c } -> vobStateOf PvClean (vobObserveShapeAll c seq.provs path seq.reasons)
    VfcObserver { channel = c } -> vobStateOf PvClean (vobObserveDeepAll c seq.provs path seq.reasons)
    VfcFence { detail = d } -> vobStateOf (vobUnknownProv env.ordinals) (appendItem (vobUnsupported op path) (appendItem (vobAbstain d) seq.reasons))
    _ -> vobStateOf (vobUnknownProv env.ordinals) (appendItem (vobAbstain "known op with no walker arm and no observer or fence class") seq.reasons)

@label "observe: shape observation over a list"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — vobObserveShape over every provenance in a positional list. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobObserveShapeAll : (channel: String) -> (ps: List ObsProv) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobObserveShapeAll channel ps path acc = case head ps of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just p -> vobObserveShapeAll channel (eufRest ps) path (vobObserveShape channel p path acc)

-- `{var: name}`. An exact binder read carries the binder's provenance. A DOTTED
-- read projects off its binder root. A spelling with no binder is either a
-- registry hit, which `resolveVar` answers with a `{$ref: id}` VALUE
-- (json-logic.ts:1613-1622), or a miss answered with the fallback — both wholly
-- literal. A dotted spelling with no binder root cannot be modelled at all and
-- abstains.
@label "observe: var use"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — a variable read: an exact binder carries its provenance, a DOTTED read projects off its binder root, and a spelling with no binder is either a registry hit (answered with a {$ref} value) or the fallback — both literal. A dotted spelling with no binder root abstains."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobVarUse : (argList: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobVarUse argList path env acc = case head argList of
  Nothing -> vobStateOf (vobUnknownProv env.ordinals) (appendItem (vobUnsupported "var" path) acc)
  Just first -> case first of
    JlString { value = name } -> vobVarNamed name path env acc
    _ -> vobStateOf (vobUnknownProv env.ordinals) (appendItem (vobUnsupported "var" path) acc)

@label "observe: var named"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — resolve one variable spelling against the lexical scope, distinguishing an exact binder read from a dotted projection off a binder root. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobVarNamed : (name: String) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: a) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobVarNamed name path env acc = case vobRootBinder env.binds name of
  Just hit ->
    if eq hit.name name
    then vobStateOf (hit.prov) (acc)
    else vobProjectDotted hit.prov path acc
  Nothing ->
    if vobIsDotted name
    then vobStateOf (vobUnknownProv env.ordinals) (appendItem (vobAbstain "dotted variable path with no binder root in scope") acc)
    else vobStateOf PvClean acc

-- `{if: [c1, t1, c2, t2, …, else?]}` / `{?:}`. The runtime evaluates conditions
-- lazily in source order and returns the first matching branch; a lone trailing
-- argument is the else branch (json-logic.ts:1643-1649).
--
-- EACH CONDITION IS A TEST, and `truthy` (json-logic.ts:2584-2590) inspects
-- primitive VALUES — `0`, `""`, `"0"`, `false`, and an EMPTY array are falsy — so
-- it is a DEEP observation, not merely an outer-shape one. A non-ground
-- condition makes branch selection instantiation-dependent.
--
-- The form's provenance is the JOIN of every reachable branch.
@label "observe: if op"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the lazy conditional: each condition is a DEEP truthy TEST (truthy inspects primitive values — zero, empty string, \"0\", false and an empty array are falsy), so a non-ground condition makes branch selection instantiation-dependent. The form's provenance is the JOIN of every reachable branch; a lone trailing argument is the else branch."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobIfOp : (argList: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobIfOp argList path env acc = vobIfPairs argList path 0 env acc [PvClean]

@label "observe: if pairs"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — walk conditional argument PAIRS in raw index order, testing each condition and joining each branch. A lone trailing argument is the else branch. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobIfPairs : (items: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (index: Nat) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> (branches: List ObsProv) -> ObsState
vobIfPairs items path index env acc branches = case head items of
  Nothing -> vobStateOf (vobJoinList branches) (acc)
  Just first ->
    if eq (length items) 1
    then
      let est = vobWalk first (appendItem (VpsArg { index = index }) path) env acc
      vobStateOf (vobJoinList (appendItem est.prov branches)) (est.reasons)
    else
      let condPath = appendItem (VpsArg { index = index }) path
      let cst = vobWalk first condPath env acc
      let tested = vobObserveDeep "branch-condition" cst.prov condPath cst.reasons
      let rest = vobTailList items
      case head rest of
        Nothing -> vobStateOf (vobJoinList (appendItem cst.prov branches)) (tested)
        Just thenNode ->
          let tst = vobWalk thenNode (appendItem (VpsArg { index = add index 1 }) path) env tested
          vobIfPairs (vobDropTwo items) path (add index 2) env tst.reasons (appendItem tst.prov branches)

-- `{and: […]}` / `{or: […]}`. These return the OPERAND VALUE, not a Boolean
-- (json-logic.ts:1863-1884), and `truthy` is applied to every operand as the
-- loop advances — so every operand is both a deep TEST and a possible result.
@label "observe: bool op"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the lazy boolean operators. They return the OPERAND VALUE rather than a Boolean, and truthy is applied to every operand, so each operand is both a deep TEST and a possible result. The form's provenance is the join of the operands."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobBoolOp : (channel: String) -> (argList: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobBoolOp channel argList path env acc =
  let seq = vobWalkArgs argList path 0 env acc []
  vobStateOf (vobJoinList seq.provs) (vobObserveDeepAll channel seq.provs path seq.reasons)

-- `{ann: [expr, type]}` strips the annotation and evaluates ONLY argument 0
-- (json-logic.ts:1436-1437). Walking the trailing type would analyse an
-- expression the runtime never evaluates.
@label "observe: ann op"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the annotation form evaluates only argument 0; the trailing type is never evaluated and contributes nothing. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobAnnOp : (argList: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobAnnOp argList path env acc = case head argList of
  Nothing -> vobStateOf (PvClean) (acc)
  Just inner -> vobWalk inner (appendItem (VpsArg { index = 0 }) path) env acc

-- `{let: {k1: v1, …}}` folds the bindings SEQUENTIALLY into a copied data
-- context, so binding i sees binders 0..i-1, and the form's value is the LAST
-- binding (there is no separate body at rest).
@label "observe: let op"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — sequential bindings folded into a copied context, so binding i sees binders 0..i-1; the form's value is the LAST binding (there is no separate body at rest)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobLetOp : (argList: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobLetOp argList path env acc =
  let layout = fdcBindingLayout "let" argList
  if not layout.total
  then vobStateOf (vobUnknownProv env.ordinals) (appendItem (vobAbstain layout.reason) acc)
  else
    let sc = vobBindings layout.entries path env acc PvClean
    vobStateOf (sc.prov) (sc.reasons)

@label "observe: bindings"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b - fold a binding entry list into the scope at VpsBinding, each value seeing the preceding binders, returning the extended scope and the LAST binding's provenance. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobBindings : (entries: [FdcBindingEntry]) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: a) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> (lastProv: ObsProv) -> ObsScopeState
vobBindings entries path env acc lastProv = case head entries of
  Nothing -> vobScopeOf (lastProv) (acc) (env.binds)
  Just e ->
    let st = vobWalk e.value (appendItem (VpsBinding { name = e.name, index = e.index }) path) env acc
    let env2 = vobEnvWith env (vobBindWith env.binds e.name st.prov)
    vobBindings (eufRest entries) path env2 st.reasons st.prov

-- `{do: [stmt, …]}`. A `{let: …}` ITEM binds into the ENCLOSING scope rather
-- than a nested one (json-logic.ts:1423-1427), which is exactly why the
-- statement fold has to thread the scope rather than the reasons alone. The
-- form's value is the last statement's.
@label "observe: do op"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — a statement sequence whose inline let items bind into the ENCLOSING scope (which is why the fold threads the scope, not the reasons alone); the form's value is the last statement's."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobDoOp : (items: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobDoOp items path env acc =
  let sc = vobDoItems items path 0 env acc PvClean
  vobStateOf (sc.prov) (sc.reasons)

@label "observe: do items"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — fold do statements at VpsSeq, threading the scope so an inline let item's binders reach the following statements. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobDoItems : (items: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (index: Nat) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> (lastProv: ObsProv) -> ObsScopeState
vobDoItems items path index env acc lastProv = case head items of
  Nothing -> vobScopeOf (lastProv) (acc) (env.binds)
  Just item ->
    let inline = fdcInlineLet item
    if not inline.present
    then
      let st = vobWalk item (appendItem (VpsSeq { index = index }) path) env acc
      vobDoItems (eufRest items) path (add index 1) env st.reasons st.prov
    else if not inline.total
    then vobDoItems (eufRest items) path (add index 1) env (appendItem (vobAbstain inline.reason) acc) (vobUnknownProv env.ordinals)
    else
      let sc = vobBindings inline.entries (appendItem (VpsSeq { index = index }) path) env acc lastProv
      vobDoItems (eufRest items) path (add index 1) (vobEnvWith env sc.binds) sc.reasons sc.prov

-- `{where: [body, bindings]}`. The runtime evaluates the bindings first into a
-- copied context, each seeing the preceding ones, and then the body
-- (json-logic.ts:1440-1447).
@label "observe: where op"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the where form: bindings first at VpsWhereBinding, each seeing the preceding ones, then the body at VpsArg 0 with every binder in scope (the runtime's order)."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobWhereOp : (argList: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobWhereOp argList path env acc =
  let layout = fdcBindingLayout "where" argList
  if not layout.present
  then vobStateOf (vobUnknownProv env.ordinals) (appendItem (vobAbstain layout.reason) acc)
  else if not layout.total
  then vobWalk layout.body (appendItem (VpsArg { index = 0 }) path) env (appendItem (vobAbstain layout.reason) acc)
  else
    let sc = vobWhereBindings layout.entries path env acc
    vobWalk layout.body (appendItem (VpsArg { index = 0 }) path) (vobEnvWith env sc.binds) sc.reasons

@label "observe: where bindings"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — fold a where clause's binding fields into the scope at VpsWhereBinding, each value seeing the preceding binders. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobWhereBindings : (entries: [FdcBindingEntry]) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: a) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsScopeState
vobWhereBindings entries path env acc = case head entries of
  Nothing -> vobScopeOf (PvClean) (acc) (env.binds)
  Just e ->
    let st = vobWalk e.value (appendItem (VpsWhereBinding { name = e.name, index = e.index }) path) env acc
    let env2 = vobEnvWith env (vobBindWith env.binds e.name st.prov)
    vobWhereBindings (eufRest entries) path env2 st.reasons

-- `{fn: [params…, body]}` builds a closure that CAPTURES the whole surrounding
-- data context (`copyOwnDataContext`, json-logic.ts:2556). Two facts follow:
--
--  1. the closure VALUE's provenance carries the capture's taint at a
--     `«capture»` slot, so handing a taint-capturing closure to a host
--     implementation fences even though the closure itself is a fixed former;
--  2. the closure's PARAMETERS are bound OPAQUELY over every ordinal in scope,
--     because the abstraction site does not know what will be supplied. Any
--     observation of a lambda parameter therefore fences here, at the
--     abstraction, rather than being deferred to an application site this slice
--     fences anyway. With no ordinals in scope the parameters are clean — with
--     nothing quantified, nothing can be κ-typed.
--
-- The lambda body's RESULT provenance is deliberately not propagated: the value
-- of a `fn` form is the closure, not its result, and every form that could apply
-- it (`apply` / `pipe` / `|>` / the raw-rule intrinsics) fences in this slice.
-- 3c models application against a summary.
@label "observe: fn op"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — a lambda CAPTURES the whole surrounding data context, so the closure value carries the capture's taint at a «capture» slot (handing a taint-capturing closure to a host implementation fences), and its PARAMETERS bind OPAQUELY over every ordinal in scope, so any observation of a parameter fences at the abstraction rather than at an application site. With no ordinals in scope the parameters are clean."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobFnOp : (argList: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobFnOp argList path env acc =
  let layout = fdcLambdaLayout argList
  let paramProv = vobUnknownProv env.ordinals
  let names = if layout.namesTotal then fdcParamSpellings layout.params [] else []
  let env2 = vobEnvWith env (vobBindParams env.binds names paramProv)
  let shell = vobShellOf "«closure»" [vobSlotOf "«capture»" (vobCaptureProv env.binds)]
  let seeded =
        if layout.namesTotal
        then acc
        else appendItem (vobAbstain "a lambda parameter spelling is not reproducible; the runtime turns the raw entry into a property key, so the binder it introduces is a spelling this analysis cannot name — and an unnamed binder does not SHADOW the outer one, which would leave a body read resolving to the wrong provenance") acc
  if not layout.bodyPresent
  then vobStateOf shell seeded
  else
    let st = vobWalk layout.body (appendItem VpsLambdaBody path) env2 seeded
    vobStateOf (shell) (st.reasons)

-- `{construct: [Name, …payload]}` builds a `$tag`-bearing record whose outer
-- former is FIXED — the primary shell producer.
--
-- `True` / `False` at arity one are the opaque-repr fast path to JS booleans
-- (json-logic.ts:1485-1486): wholly literal.
--
-- THE NAMED-VS-POSITIONAL READING IS AMBIGUOUS WITHOUT THE CONSTRUCTOR TABLE.
-- `applyOp` decides it from the registered field names (json-logic.ts:1510-1530),
-- which a pure body does not have. So a single plain-object payload contributes
-- BOTH readings' slots: the positional `_0` AND every one of that record's own
-- field keys. The slot set is then a SUPERSET of the real one, so any real key
-- resolves to a provenance at least as tainted as the truth — over-tainting,
-- never under-tainting.
@label "observe: construct op"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the primary shell producer: a constructed value's outer former is fixed and its payload slots carry the arguments' provenances. True/False at arity one are the opaque-repr fast path to JS booleans and are wholly literal. The named-versus-positional payload reading needs the constructor table a pure body lacks, so a single plain-object payload contributes BOTH readings' slots — a SUPERSET, so any real key resolves to a provenance at least as tainted as the truth."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobConstructOp : (argList: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobConstructOp argList path env acc =
  let layout = fdcCtorLayout argList
  if not layout.namePresent
  then vobStateOf (vobUnknownProv env.ordinals) (appendItem (vobUnsupported "construct" path) acc)
  else if layout.boolFastPath
  then vobStateOf PvClean acc
  else if eq (length layout.payload) 0
  then vobStateOf (vobShellOf layout.name []) acc
  else vobConstructPayload layout.name layout path env acc

@label "observe: construct payload"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — walk a constructor's payload into shell slots: positional keys always, plus the named-record reading's own field keys when the payload is a single plain object (the ambiguity a pure body cannot resolve). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobConstructPayload : (name: String) -> (layout: FdcCtorLayout) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobConstructPayload name layout path env acc =
  let seq = vobWalkArgs layout.payload path 1 env acc []
  let positional = vobPositionalSlots seq.provs 0 []
  let named = vobNamedPayloadSlots layout.namedFields path env seq.reasons
  vobStateOf (vobShellOf name (vobMergeSlots positional named.slots)) named.reasons

@label "observe: merge slots"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — merge two slot lists by JOINING colliding keys rather than letting the first hit win. Load-bearing for the constructor dual reading: a named payload carrying a `_0` field collides with the positional reading's own `_0`, and first-hit lookup would answer with the whole-record shell while the runtime's named branch stores the payload directly — masking that payload's provenance. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobMergeSlots : (la: List ObsProvSlot) -> (lb: List ObsProvSlot) -> List ObsProvSlot
vobMergeSlots la lb = vobJoinSlots la lb

@label "observe: positional slots"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the positional payload slots (_0, _1, …) for a constructor's arguments. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobPositionalSlots : (ps: List ObsProv) -> (index: Nat) -> (acc: List ObsProvSlot) -> List ObsProvSlot
vobPositionalSlots ps index acc = case head ps of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just p ->
    vobPositionalSlots (eufRest ps) (add index 1) (appendItem (ObsProvSlot { key = vobPositionalKey index, prov = p }) acc)

-- The named-record reading's slots. SLICE 3e: the SHAPE test moved to the
-- shared `fdcCtorLayout`, which publishes the field list whenever the payload is
-- exactly one OBJECT — a `$tag`-bearing and a `$`-keyed one INCLUDED, because
-- `applyOp`'s named test is any non-null non-array object and, with a registered
-- `ctorDef` declaring a `$`-spelled field, that branch really is taken. This
-- file previously excluded both shapes locally and so lost the slots the runtime
-- would have filled.
@label "observe: named payload slots"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3e — the named-record reading's payload slots, over the field list the SHARED constructor layout publishes. The shape test lives there, and it admits any single-object payload — a $tag-bearing and a $-keyed one included — because applyOp's named test is any non-null non-array object. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobNamedPayloadSlots : (fields: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> a
vobNamedPayloadSlots fields path env acc =
  if eq (length fields) 0
  then { slots = [], reasons = acc }
  else vobNamedFieldSlots fields path env [] acc

@label "observe: named field slots"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the payload slots for a named-record constructor payload, keyed by field name. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobNamedFieldSlots : (fields: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ObsProvSlot) -> (reasons: List ValidationReason) -> c
-- KEEPS its reasons. An earlier draft discarded them on the premise that the
-- positional pass walks the same expressions — FALSE, and the round-2 review
-- produced the counterexample: for an op-shaped ONE-FIELD payload record such as
-- `{construct:["R",{ann:[0,{length:{var:"x"}}]}]}`, the runtime's NAMED branch
-- evaluates the whole field value while the positional reading sees an `ann`
-- form and evaluates argument 0 only. The observation lives on the named side,
-- so throwing its reasons away lost it. Duplicate reasons across the two
-- readings are harmless (a fence is a fence); a lost one is not.
vobNamedFieldSlots fields path env acc reasons = case head fields of
  Nothing -> { slots = acc, reasons = reasons }
  Just f ->
    let st = vobWalk f.value (appendItem (VpsField { key = f.name }) path) env reasons
    vobNamedFieldSlots (eufRest fields) path env (appendItem (ObsProvSlot { key = f.name, prov = st.prov }) acc) st.reasons

-- `{call: [head, …args]}`. Only a LITERAL name head reaches the gate: the `$`
-- application head (json-logic.ts:2436-2440) and a callee that is an expression
-- or a `{var}` are dynamic applications whose target is a VALUE, so no frozen
-- target record can describe them.
@label "observe: call op"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the explicit application form. Only a LITERAL name head reaches the call gate; the $ application head and an expression or {var} callee are dynamic applications whose target is a VALUE, so no frozen target record can describe them."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobCallOp : (argList: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobCallOp argList path env acc =
  let layout = fdcCallLayout "call" argList
  case layout.callee of
    FdcCalleeName { name = h } ->
      let seq = vobWalkSlots layout.slots path env acc []
      vobGateCall h seq.provs path env seq.reasons
    FdcCalleeDollar -> vobDollarCall layout path env acc
    _ -> vobDynamicCall "call" argList path env acc

@label "observe: dynamic call"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — a dynamic application: the arguments are still walked so no nested observation is lost, and the form fences because the callee identity is a value rather than an exact target. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobDynamicCall : (form: String) -> (items: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobDynamicCall form items path env acc =
  let seq = vobWalkArgs items path 0 env acc []
  vobStateOf (vobUnknownProv env.ordinals) (appendItem (RsnDynamicOrReflectiveUse { useId = form, detail = "callee identity is a value, not an exact target" }) seq.reasons)

-- `{method: [Class, name, …args]}` — the use-site QUALIFIED dispatch form. The
-- dispatch argument is reflected to select the instance, so the gate is entered
-- with the method's raw key and the frozen record's `RDispatch` route carries the
-- position.
@label "observe: method op"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — use-site qualified dispatch. The dispatch argument is reflected to select the instance, so the gate is entered with the method's raw key and the frozen record's RDispatch route carries the position."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobMethodOp : (argList: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobMethodOp argList path env acc =
  let layout = fdcCallLayout "method" argList
  case layout.callee of
    FdcCalleeName { name = m } ->
      let seq = vobWalkSlots layout.slots path env acc []
      vobGateCall (vobMethodKey argList m) seq.provs path env seq.reasons
    _ -> vobStateOf (vobUnknownProv env.ordinals) (appendItem (vobUnsupported "method" path) acc)

@label "observe: key as fnId"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the key-as-fnId call form, the universal call shape and the only route to BUILTIN_OP_NATIVES. The runtime decides call-versus-record by RESOLUTION rather than value shape, so a key with no frozen target record is an unresolved use, never silently a record literal."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobKeyAsFnId : (op: String) -> (argList: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobKeyAsFnId op argList path env acc =
  let seq = vobWalkArgs argList path 0 env acc []
  vobGateCall op seq.provs path env seq.reasons

-- =========================================================================
-- the pattern rules (M1-M6 — the finding-1 grammar, not the four-case ADT)
-- =========================================================================

-- `{match: [scrutinee, p1, b1, p2, b2, …, else?]}` (json-logic.ts:1651-1677).
@label "observe: match op"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the match form: walk the scrutinee, then each arm's pattern against the scrutinee's provenance, its guard as a deep TEST in the arm-extended scope, and its body. A lone trailing element is the default arm body, evaluated in the OUTER scope. The form's provenance is the join of the arm bodies."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobMatchOp : (argList: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobMatchOp argList path env acc =
  let layout = fdcMatchLayout argList
  if not layout.scrutineePresent
  then vobStateOf (PvClean) (acc)
  else
    let sst = vobWalk layout.scrutinee (appendItem VpsScrutinee path) env acc
    let armed = vobMatchArms layout.arms path env sst.reasons sst.prov [PvClean]
    if not layout.fallbackPresent
    then vobStateOf (vobJoinList armed.provs) (armed.reasons)
    else
      let dst = vobWalk layout.fallback (appendItem (VpsArmBody { index = layout.fallbackIndex }) path) env armed.reasons
      vobStateOf (vobJoinList (appendItem dst.prov armed.provs)) (dst.reasons)

@label "observe: match arms"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b - fold the shared layout's arms: the pattern against the scrutinee's provenance, then the guard at VpsArmGuard as a deep TEST in the arm-extended scope, then the body at VpsArmBody. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobMatchArms : (arms: [FdcMatchArm]) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: a) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> (scrutProv: ObsProv) -> (branches: List ObsProv) -> ObsProvList
vobMatchArms arms path env acc scrutProv branches = case head arms of
  Nothing -> vobProvListOf (branches) (acc)
  Just arm ->
    let seeded =
          if fdcPatternBindsTotal arm.pattern
          then acc
          else appendItem (vobAbstain "an arm pattern introduces a binder this analysis may not install: either its runtime spelling is not reproducible, or its write is CONDITIONAL on the scrutinee — the Boolean-representation arm matches a True/False tag pattern against a native boolean and returns an EMPTY binding set before the structural arm runs, so installing it unconditionally would give a body read the scrutinee's provenance where the runtime gives it the outer binder's") acc
    let pat = vobPattern arm.pattern scrutProv (appendItem (VpsArmPattern { index = arm.index }) path) seeded
    let envArm = vobEnvWith env (vobBindAll env.binds pat.binds)
    let afterGuard = vobWalkGuard arm path envArm pat.reasons
    let bst = vobWalk arm.body (appendItem (VpsArmBody { index = arm.index }) path) envArm afterGuard
    vobMatchArms (eufRest arms) path env bst.reasons scrutProv (appendItem bst.prov branches)

-- A guard is an arbitrary expression evaluated in the arm-extended context and
-- then `truthy`-tested (json-logic.ts:1672), so its RESULT is a deep test
-- exactly like a conditional's condition. The SPLIT itself — a top-level
-- ARRAY-valued `$guard` on either carrier — is the shared decomposition's.
@label "observe: walk guard"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b - walk a guarded arm's condition at VpsArmGuard in the arm-extended scope; its result is truthy-tested, so it is a DEEP test exactly like a conditional's condition. An unguarded arm contributes nothing. The guard SPLIT comes from the shared decomposition. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobWalkGuard : (arm: FdcMatchArm) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: a) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobWalkGuard arm path env acc =
  if arm.guarded
  then
    let gpath = appendItem (VpsArmGuard { index = arm.index }) path
    let gst = vobWalk arm.guard gpath env acc
    vobObserveDeep "arm-guard" gst.prov gpath gst.reasons
  else acc

-- vobPattern — the M1-M6 rules of `matchPattern`, in the runtime's own order.
--
--  M1 the wildcard `"_"` matches everything and binds nothing: NO observation.
--  M2 a `$bind`-bearing object binds the WHOLE scrutinee and is checked before
--     any structural arm, so it too observes nothing — it merely propagates the
--     scrutinee's provenance to the binder.
--  M3 host identity (`pattern === scrutinee`) compares a LITERAL against the
--     value with raw JS identity: a DEEP observation.
--  M4 the Boolean representation coercion equates a `True`/`False` tag pattern
--     with a native JS boolean scrutinee: a representation observation, covered
--     by M5's rule since the pattern is a tagged object.
--  M5 a structural object pattern REQUIRES the scrutinee to carry each pattern
--     key (`ownDataRead(...).found` or the match fails) and recurses. That is a
--     key-presence plus discriminator observation of the OUTER former, so it is
--     admissible on a clean value and on a shell — and fences on an opaque one.
--  M6 the fall-through observes nothing (the match simply fails).
@label "observe: pattern"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — classify one RAW pattern against a scrutinee's provenance by matchPattern's own six arms, not by the four-case surface Pattern ADT. The wildcard and a $bind pattern observe nothing; a literal pattern is a DEEP host-identity comparison; a structural object or array pattern is a key-presence plus discriminator observation of the OUTER former, admissible on a clean value or a shell and fencing on an opaque one."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobPattern : (pattern: (JsonLogic Any)) -> (prov: ObsProv) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsPatOutcome
vobPattern pattern prov path acc =
  let plan = fdcPatternPlan pattern
  vobPatSteps plan.steps prov path acc

-- SLICE 3e — the arm SELECTION comes from the shared plan, in the runtime's
-- own order; what each arm OBSERVES stays here. A plan whose terminal step is
-- the wildcard or a `$bind` observes nothing; an identity-only plan is a DEEP
-- host comparison against a literal; the structural plans are a key-presence
-- plus discriminator observation of the OUTER former.
@label "observe: pattern steps"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3e - map the shared pattern plan's ordered matcher steps onto their observations. The wildcard and $bind steps observe nothing; an identity-only plan is a DEEP host-identity comparison against a literal; the field and item steps are a key-presence plus discriminator observation of the OUTER former. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobPatSteps : (steps: [FdcPatternStep]) -> (prov: ObsProv) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsPatOutcome
vobPatSteps steps prov path acc = case head steps of
  Nothing -> vobPatOf (vobIsGround prov) [] (vobObserveDeep "pattern-literal" prov path acc)
  Just step -> case step of
    FdcPatWildcard -> vobPatOf true [] acc
    FdcPatBind { name = n } -> vobBindArm n prov acc
    FdcPatFields { fields = fs } -> vobPatternStructural fs prov path (vobObserveShape (vobPatChannel fs) prov path acc) []
    FdcPatItems { items = xs } -> vobPatternItems xs prov path acc [] 0
    _ -> vobPatSteps (eufRest steps) prov path acc

-- The channel distinguishes a TAGGED carrier from a plain one, and the shared
-- plan already answers it: the marshaller only produces a tagged carrier for a
-- literal-string `$tag`, and the plan reconstructs exactly that entry with the
-- WIRE role. So a wire-role field present ⟺ the carrier was tagged.
@label "observe: pattern channel"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3e - the observation channel for a structural pattern: pattern-tag when the plan carries a WIRE discriminator field (which happens exactly when the carrier was a tagged one), pattern-structural otherwise. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobPatChannel : (fields: [FdcPatField]) -> String
vobPatChannel fields = case head fields of
  Nothing -> "pattern-structural"
  Just f -> case f.role of
    FdcPatRoleWireTag -> "pattern-tag"
    _ -> vobPatChannel (eufRest fields)

-- 3d-D4 — the `$bind` ARM, and why it is now shared by BOTH object arms.
-- `matchPattern` reads `$bind` off ANY object with `ownDataRead` and returns
-- IMMEDIATELY, before every structural arm (json-logic.ts:1818-1821). A
-- marshalled `JlTagged` carrier is still such an object, so recognizing `$bind`
-- only on `JlObject` let a `{$tag: …, $bind: …}` pattern take the STRUCTURAL
-- path here while the runtime took the bind path — the analysis modelling a
-- different arm than the one that runs.
--
-- The non-literal case ABSTAINS as well as binding. The runtime names the
-- binder `String(value)` (json-logic.ts:1820), and this analysis deliberately
-- does not reproduce that coercion — a cloned decider context BOXES host
-- numbers, so a Fenel-side rendering of one is the recorded `[object Object]`
-- landmine. 3b introduced a binder under a SYNTHETIC spelling so the arm's
-- shape stayed right; the gap that repair left is that a later `{var: "0"}`
-- read finds no binder at the synthetic name. Binding AND abstaining keeps the
-- 3b shape and closes the gap: the arm can no longer admit.
@label "observe: bind arm"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the $bind pattern arm, shared by the tagged and plain object arms because matchPattern reads $bind off ANY object and returns before every structural arm (json-logic.ts:1818-1821). A literal name binds the whole scrutinee and observes nothing; a NON-literal one binds a synthetic spelling AND abstains, because the runtime names the binder String(value) and this analysis does not reproduce that coercion (rendering a boxed host number is the recorded landmine), so a later read of the real name would find no binder."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobBindArm : (name: FdcParamName) -> (prov: ObsProv) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsPatOutcome
vobBindArm name prov acc =
  if fdcNameExact name
  then vobPatOf true [ObsBind { name = fdcNameSpelling name, prov = prov }] acc
  else vobPatOf true [ObsBind { name = "«non-literal-bind»", prov = prov }] (appendItem (vobAbstain "a non-literal $bind names its binder by the runtime's String() coercion, which this analysis does not reproduce, so a later read of the real spelling would find no binder") acc)

-- The structural arm over a pattern's fields. A WIRE `$tag` — one whose pattern
-- value is a literal string — is a DISCRIMINATOR read, already charged as an
-- outer-shape observation by the caller and never recursed into (the runtime
-- compares two strings there). EVERY OTHER KEY, `$guard` and a non-string
-- `$tag` INCLUDED, is an ordinary payload read at that slot.
--
-- 3d-D4 narrowed both skips, because the runtime's skips are narrower than 3b's
-- were:
--  * `$guard` is stripped by `matchOp` only when it is TOP-LEVEL and
--    ARRAY-valued; `vobGuardParts` already removes exactly that case, so any
--    `$guard` still present when this fold sees it is a field the runtime
--    MATCHES — and a match requires the scrutinee to carry the key. Skipping it
--    dropped both the key-presence requirement and the sub-pattern's own
--    observations.
--  * `$tag` reaches `constructorPatternWireName`, which returns a NON-string
--    value UNCHANGED and then recurses `matchPattern` on it like any other
--    field (json-logic.ts). Skipping it dropped a deep comparison.
@label "observe: pattern structural"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the structural pattern arm over a pattern's fields. A WIRE $tag (literal-string pattern value) is a discriminator read already charged as an outer-shape observation and never recursed into; EVERY other key — $guard and a non-string $tag included — is an ordinary payload read at that slot. 3b skipped both keys unconditionally, which was wider than the runtime: matchOp strips only a top-level ARRAY-valued $guard (vobGuardParts already removes exactly that), and a non-string $tag is returned unchanged by constructorPatternWireName and then matched like any other field. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobPatternStructural : (fields: [FdcPatField]) -> (prov: ObsProv) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> (binds: List ObsBind) -> ObsPatOutcome
vobPatternStructural fields prov path acc binds = case head fields of
  Nothing -> vobPatOf (vobShapeFixed prov) (binds) (acc)
  Just f -> case f.role of
    FdcPatRoleWireTag -> vobPatternStructural (eufRest fields) prov path acc binds
    FdcPatRolePayload ->
      let slot = vobProject prov f.key (appendItem (VpsPatternField { key = f.key }) path) acc
      let sub = vobPattern f.value slot.prov (appendItem (VpsPatternField { key = f.key }) path) slot.reasons
      vobPatternStructural (eufRest fields) prov path sub.reasons (vobBindAll binds sub.binds)

-- An ARRAY pattern is structural too: `typeof [] === "object"`, so `matchPattern`
-- takes the same arm and iterates the array's own index keys. The scrutinee's
-- element provenance is the shell's `«element»` slot.
@label "observe: pattern items"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — an array pattern is structural (an array is an object, so matchPattern takes the same arm and iterates index keys); each item is matched against the shell's «element» slot provenance. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobPatternItems : (items: a) -> (prov: ObsProv) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> (binds: List ObsBind) -> (index: Nat) -> ObsPatOutcome
vobPatternItems items prov path acc binds index = case head items of
  Nothing -> vobPatOf (vobShapeFixed prov) (binds) (vobObserveShape "pattern-array" prov path acc)
  Just item ->
    let elem = vobProject prov "«element»" (appendItem (VpsPatternArg { index = index }) path) acc
    let sub = vobPattern item elem.prov (appendItem (VpsPatternArg { index = index }) path) elem.reasons
    vobPatternItems (eufRest items) prov path sub.reasons (vobBindAll binds sub.binds) (add index 1)

-- =========================================================================
-- 3b-D5 — the frozen execution-profile scope, and the public entry
-- =========================================================================

-- A verdict with no profile qualifier is a latent unsoundness the moment the
-- other lowering runs: `eq` and `lt` lower to host `===` and `<` in compiled JS
-- (emit-js.fenel's `callMappingOf`) while the interpreted path runs the
-- type-discriminated structural `eq`. Both are representation-sensitive, so an
-- observation fence on them is profile-INDEPENDENT — the safe direction — but
-- the qualifier is mandatory rather than derived, because a future divergence
-- need not land on the safe side.
--
-- STRICT v1: a verdict is admissible only when the analysed profile set COVERS
-- every profile the registration can run under.
@label "observe: profile gate"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the frozen execution-profile scope. A verdict with no profile qualifier is a latent unsoundness the moment the other lowering runs (eq and lt lower to host === and < in compiled JS while the interpreted path runs type-discriminated structural equality). Strict v1: admissible only when the analysed profile set COVERS every profile the registration can run under."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobProfileGate : (analysed: List String) -> (required: List String) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobProfileGate analysed required acc = case head required of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just r ->
    let next = if vobNameIn analysed r
          then acc
          else appendItem (vobAbstain "execution profile not covered by this verdict") acc
    vobProfileGate analysed (eufRest required) next

@label "observe: is known op"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — is this raw key one of the evaluator's KNOWN_OPS (as opposed to a key-as-fnId call head)? Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobIsKnownOp : (op: String) -> Boolean
vobIsKnownOp op = fdcIsKnownOp op

-- =========================================================================
-- 3d-D3 — THE EXECUTION MODE, on its two independent axes
--
-- 3b carried ONE `profile` string, which conflated three orthogonal questions:
-- WHICH REGISTRY the function came from (SYSTEM / seed), WHICH LOWERING runs
-- (interpreted / compiled-js / …), and WHICH EVALUATOR ENTRY invokes it
-- (the direct call, a scoped `Evaluator` strategy, an explicit `evaluateWith`).
-- That conflation is why `obs.gate.ambient` could read as a claim about the
-- whole engine when it is a claim about `invokeFunction`: an evaluator STRATEGY
-- calls the ctx-natives map directly after parking the caller's data in
-- `ctx._localData` (`evaluator-class.ts`'s `makeStrategyWrapper`), so it never
-- passes through `invokeFunction`'s selection order at all.
--
-- STRICT v1 ADMITS ONE MODE: the interpreted lowering under the DIRECT
-- evaluator entry. Everything else — every compiled lowering, every scoped
-- strategy including a scoped Eager frame, and explicit `evaluateWith` — is
-- enumerated and NOT admissible. An unrecognized string is not admissible
-- either, and that is the important half: a whitelist can only reject a typo,
-- so the gate must fence what it does not recognize rather than treat an
-- unknown mode as the default one.
--
-- WHAT THIS GATE CANNOT DO. Evaluator strategies are registry-OPEN — there is
-- no closed runtime strategy ADT — so this enumeration cannot claim to name the
-- runtime universe. It claims only that a verdict is scoped to the ONE mode it
-- names, and a consumer must re-establish that the execution it is about to
-- trust IS that mode. The enumeration is a scope declaration, not a survey.
-- =========================================================================

@label "observe: known lowerings"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the lowering axis of the execution mode. Interpreted versus a compiled target is a DIFFERENT question from which evaluator entry runs; 3b's single profile string conflated them."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobKnownLowerings : (unit: Any) -> List String
vobKnownLowerings unit = ["interpreted", "compiled-js", "compiled-wasm", "compiled-llvm"]

@label "observe: known evaluators"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the evaluator-ENTRY axis of the execution mode: the direct call, a scoped Evaluator strategy frame (Eager / Lazy / Partial / Jit / a user-registered one), or an explicit evaluateWith. A scoped strategy calls the ctx-natives map directly after parking caller data in ctx._localData, so it never passes through invokeFunction's selection order — which is why the ambient gate needs this axis. Strategies are registry-OPEN, so this list is a scope declaration, not a survey of the runtime universe."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobKnownEvaluators : (unit: Any) -> List String
vobKnownEvaluators unit =
  [ "Direct", "ScopedEager", "ScopedLazy", "ScopedPartial", "ScopedJit"
  , "ScopedCustom", "ExplicitEvaluateWith"
  ]

@label "observe: mode gate"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the top-level execution-mode fence. Strict v1 admits ONLY the interpreted lowering under the DIRECT evaluator entry; every compiled lowering, every scoped strategy (a scoped Eager frame included, since its context still carries the frame) and explicit evaluateWith abstain, and an UNRECOGNIZED mode abstains rather than defaulting — the half that matters, because a whitelist can otherwise only reject a typo."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobModeGate : (lowering: String) -> (evaluator: String) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobModeGate lowering evaluator acc =
  let afterLowering =
        if not (vobNameIn (vobKnownLowerings 0) lowering)
        then appendItem (vobAbstain "unrecognized lowering: a verdict is scoped to the lowering it names and an unknown one is not the default one") acc
        else if not (eq lowering "interpreted")
        then appendItem (vobAbstain "strict v1 covers the interpreted lowering only; a compiled lowering runs different primitives for the representation-sensitive operations") acc
        else acc
  if not (vobNameIn (vobKnownEvaluators 0) evaluator)
  then appendItem (vobAbstain "unrecognized evaluator entry: evaluator strategies are registry-open, so an unknown entry is not the direct one") afterLowering
  else if not (eq evaluator "Direct")
  then appendItem (vobAbstain "strict v1 covers the DIRECT evaluator entry only; a scoped strategy calls the ctx-natives map with a context carrying parked caller data, bypassing invokeFunction's selection order entirely") afterLowering
  else afterLowering

-- 3d ROUND-2 REPAIR — THE MODE AND THE PUBLISHED LABEL WERE TWO AUTHORITIES.
--
-- `ObsAdmitted` republishes `analysedProfiles` VERBATIM, and nothing tied that
-- list to the mode the request declared. So a request could name
-- `lowering = "interpreted"` and `evaluator = "Direct"` — passing the mode gate
-- — while carrying `analysedProfiles = ["compiled-js"]`, and the admission came
-- back LABELLED as covering the compiled lowering. Nothing compiled had been
-- analysed. An arbitrary string worked too, because `vobProfileGate` only
-- checks that each REQUIRED profile appears in the ANALYSED list and never asks
-- what a profile IS.
--
-- The repair is to make the lowering the single authority: every analysed and
-- every required profile must BE the declared lowering. That is the honest
-- reading of what this slice analyses — one mode, named once — and it closes
-- the label channel without inventing a profile algebra the slice does not have.
@label "observe: profile label gate"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — bind the PUBLISHED profile label to the declared execution mode. ObsAdmitted republishes analysedProfiles verbatim and nothing tied that list to the mode, so a request could pass the mode gate on interpreted/Direct while labelling its admission `compiled-js` — a verdict claiming coverage of a lowering nothing analysed. Every analysed and required profile must now BE the declared lowering."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobProfileLabelGate : (lowering: String) -> (profiles: List String) -> (role: String) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobProfileLabelGate lowering profiles role acc = case head profiles of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just p ->
    let next = if eq p lowering
          then acc
          else appendItem (vobAbstain (concat role " profile set names a profile that is not the declared lowering, so the verdict would publish coverage of a mode nothing was analysed under")) acc
    vobProfileLabelGate lowering (eufRest profiles) role next

-- =========================================================================
-- 3d-D3 — the FROZEN CALL TARGET's own well-formedness
--
-- `ObsCallTarget` is an EXTERNAL record. 3b read `tier` with
-- `vobIsCtxTier`, which answers FALSE for anything it does not recognize — so a
-- misspelled or absent tier silently skipped the ambient fence. Validating the
-- coordinate closes that direction.
--
-- IT DOES NOT CLOSE THE OTHER ONE, and the row says so: a whitelist rejects a
-- typo, not a LIE. A record that calls a genuine ctx-native `nativeImpls` is
-- well-formed and wrong, and so is an under-stated `resultRigids`. Those are
-- the authenticated producer's obligation, not this gate's.
-- =========================================================================

@label "observe: branch is native-mapped"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — is this branch reached THROUGH one of the two native maps? A strictly narrower question than vobBranchIsHostActive: HostNative and NativeWithFallback are, while ExternalHandler (a declaration with no installed implementation) and BuiltinOpNative (reached only for a key with no registration at all) are host-active but carry NO native-map coordinate. Conflating the two false-fenced correct records. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobBranchIsNativeMapped : (origin: String) -> Boolean
vobBranchIsNativeMapped origin =
  if eq origin "HostNative" then true else eq origin "NativeWithFallback"

@label "observe: known tiers"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the closed native-map coordinate set: the empty string (no native map — a Fenel body or an external handler), the two real maps, and `both` for a key registered in each. Anything else is malformed."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobKnownTiers : (unit: Any) -> List String
vobKnownTiers unit = ["", "nativeImplsCtx", "nativeImpls", "both"]

@label "observe: target issues"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — validate a frozen call-target record against the closed coordinate sets and the check scope's ranges: an unrecognized tier, a tier inconsistent with the origin (a Fenel body or external handler naming a native map, or a host native naming none), a resultRigids ordinal outside the scope, and a summary index outside the declared arity all ABSTAIN. 3b read the tier with a predicate that answered false for anything unrecognized, so a misspelled tier silently skipped the ambient fence. This rejects malformation, NOT misstatement: a record calling a genuine ctx-native `nativeImpls` is well-formed and wrong, which is the authenticated producer's obligation."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobTargetIssues : (t: ObsCallTarget) -> (ordinals: List Nat) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobTargetIssues t ordinals acc =
  -- 3d ROUND-2 REPAIR — the consistency rule used the WRONG PARTITION, and it
  -- false-fenced live records. `vobBranchIsHostActive` is the ACTIVE-HOST
  -- predicate: it admits `ExternalHandler` and `BuiltinOpNative` alongside
  -- `HostNative` / `NativeWithFallback`. But only the last two are reached
  -- THROUGH A NATIVE MAP — an external handler is a declaration with no
  -- installed implementation, and a `BuiltinOpNative` is reached only for a key
  -- with no registration at all (json-logic.ts). Both legitimately carry the
  -- empty coordinate, so demanding one of every host-active origin abstained on
  -- correct records. The rule needs the NATIVE-MAP partition, which is a
  -- different question from "is this an active host implementation".
  let afterTier =
        if not (vobNameIn (vobKnownTiers 0) t.tier)
        then appendItem (vobAbstain "frozen call target names an unrecognized native-map coordinate") acc
        else if vobBranchIsNativeMapped t.origin
        then (if eq t.tier "" then appendItem (vobAbstain "frozen call target claims a native-map implementation branch but names no native-map coordinate") acc else acc)
        else (if eq t.tier "" then acc else appendItem (vobAbstain "frozen call target names a native-map coordinate for a branch that is not reached through a native map") acc)
  let afterRigids =
        if vobCoversOrdinals ordinals t.resultRigids
        then afterTier
        else appendItem (vobAbstain "frozen call target's result ordinals name a quantifier outside this check scope") afterTier
  case t.summary of
    Nothing -> afterRigids
    Just s ->
      let afterObserves = if vobIndicesInRange s.observesFrom s.paramCount then afterRigids else appendItem (vobAbstain "summary names an observed parameter index outside its own declared arity") afterRigids
      if vobIndicesInRange s.outputDerivesFrom s.paramCount
      then afterObserves
      else appendItem (vobAbstain "summary names an output-derivation index outside its own declared arity") afterObserves

@label "observe: indices in range"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — are every one of these parameter indices below the declared bound? Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobIndicesInRange : (idxs: List Nat) -> (bound: Nat) -> Boolean
vobIndicesInRange idxs bound = case head idxs of
  Nothing -> true
  Just i -> if lt i bound then vobIndicesInRange (eufRest idxs) bound else false

@label "observe: names distinct"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — are these spellings pairwise distinct and all non-empty? Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobNamesDistinct : (names: List String) -> (seen: List String) -> Boolean
vobNamesDistinct names seen = case head names of
  Nothing -> true
  Just n ->
    if eq n ""
    then false
    else if vobNameIn seen n
    then false
    else vobNamesDistinct (eufRest names) (appendItem n seen)

@label "observe: param names"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the binder spellings of a declared parameter list. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobParamNames : (ps: List ObsParam) -> (acc: List String) -> List String
vobParamNames ps acc = case head ps of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just p -> vobParamNames (eufRest ps) (appendItem p.name acc)

@label "observe: quantifier source names"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the SOURCE spellings of a quantifier vector (the namespace a compatibility $var node resolves against). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobQuantifierSourceNames : (qs: List ObsQuantifier) -> (acc: List String) -> List String
vobQuantifierSourceNames qs acc = case head qs of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just q -> vobQuantifierSourceNames (eufRest qs) (appendItem q.sourceName acc)

@label "observe: quantifier ids"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the GENERATED identities of a quantifier vector (the namespace the authoritative application sidecar resolves against). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobQuantifierIds : (qs: List ObsQuantifier) -> (acc: List String) -> List String
vobQuantifierIds qs acc = case head qs of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just q -> vobQuantifierIds (eufRest qs) (appendItem q.id acc)

-- The request's own well-formedness. Every check here is one a caller could
-- otherwise use to make the check scope look SMALLER than it is:
--
--  * a duplicate parameter spelling means one of the two provenances is
--    unreachable through `vobBindLookup`, so the tainted one can be hidden
--    behind a clean one;
--  * a duplicate or empty quantifier SOURCE spelling makes
--    `vobQuantifierOrdinal` answer for the wrong binder or for none;
--  * a duplicate or empty generated ID breaks the identity the sidecar keys on;
--  * an empty invalidation-identity field leaves the verdict bound to nothing.
--
-- The identity fields are checked for PRESENCE, not recomputed from the body.
-- That distinction is the honest one: they let a consumer bind this verdict to
-- a registration, they do not authenticate the request against one.
@label "observe: request issues"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the frozen request's own well-formedness: a duplicate parameter spelling (which hides one provenance behind another), a duplicate or empty quantifier source name or generated id, an empty analysed-profile set, and an empty invalidation-identity field each ABSTAIN. Every one is a channel for making the check scope look smaller than it is. The identity fields are checked for PRESENCE and never recomputed from the body — they BIND the verdict for a consumer to re-establish, they do not authenticate the request."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobRequestIssues : (request: ObsRequest) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobRequestIssues request acc =
  let afterIdentity =
        if eq request.callerId "" then appendItem (vobAbstain "frozen request carries no caller identity") acc
        else if eq request.bodyHash "" then appendItem (vobAbstain "frozen request carries no body hash to bind the verdict to") acc
        else if eq request.schemeHash "" then appendItem (vobAbstain "frozen request carries no scheme hash to bind the verdict to") acc
        else if eq request.validatorVersion "" then appendItem (vobAbstain "frozen request carries no validator version") acc
        else if eq request.registryProfile "" then appendItem (vobAbstain "frozen request carries no registry profile") acc
        else acc
  let afterParams =
        if vobNamesDistinct (vobParamNames request.params []) []
        then afterIdentity
        else appendItem (vobAbstain "declared parameter spellings are not pairwise distinct and non-empty, so one parameter's provenance would be unreachable behind another's") afterIdentity
  let afterSources =
        if vobNamesDistinct (vobQuantifierSourceNames request.quantified []) []
        then afterParams
        else appendItem (vobAbstain "quantifier source spellings are not pairwise distinct and non-empty, so a $var node would resolve to the wrong binder or to none") afterParams
  let afterIds =
        if vobNamesDistinct (vobQuantifierIds request.quantified []) []
        then afterSources
        else appendItem (vobAbstain "quantifier generated identities are not pairwise distinct and non-empty") afterSources
  if eq (length request.analysedProfiles) 0
  then appendItem (vobAbstain "frozen request names no analysed profile, so the verdict would cover nothing") afterIds
  else afterIds

-- vobAnalyze — THE PUBLIC ENTRY (3d-D1). Walks one RAW stored body under one
-- frozen request and reports either the complete fence set or the body's result
-- provenance with the profiles the verdict covers.
--
-- WHAT CHANGED FROM 3b, AND WHY IT IS THE POINT OF THE SLICE. 3b took
-- `params : List ObsBind` and `ordinals : List Nat`, so both the parameter
-- PROVENANCE and the size of the check scope were the caller's to state. That
-- made `obs.shell.complete` a CONTRACT rather than an invariant: a caller could
-- hand in a shell whose slots omitted the tainted payload, and `vobIsGround`
-- — which recurses only through MODELLED slots — would read it as ground and
-- admit every deep observation of it. Now the request carries DECLARED TYPES
-- and the QUANTIFIER VECTOR; the provenance and the ordinal set are both
-- derived here. No caller-controlled parameter seed reaches the walker.
--
-- WHAT IS STILL ATTESTED, stated so the ledger row does not over-claim. The
-- declared types, the quantifier vector, the frozen targets and the identity
-- hashes are all still SUPPLIED. This entry checks their well-formedness and
-- derives everything downstream of them; it does not authenticate them against
-- a registration. And the body walker itself still BUILDS shells (an array
-- literal, a record literal, a constructor payload, a closure capture), so the
-- right statement is "no caller-controlled parameter-seed shell reaches the
-- production entry", never "no shell is constructible".
--
-- **`targets` IS STILL A PROVENANCE CHANNEL, and the PARAMETER seed is the only
-- one this slice closed.** A frozen `ObsCallTarget` carries `resultRigids`, and
-- a summary carries `outputDerivesFrom` / `observesFrom`; `vobCallOutput` mints
-- the call's RESULT provenance from exactly those. `vobTargetIssues` rejects an
-- ordinal OUTSIDE the check scope but cannot detect an OMITTED one, so an
-- under-stated `resultRigids` yields a clean result for a call that returns κ,
-- and a summary declaring `observesFrom = []` authorizes a callee that observes
-- everything. Both are attestations. A consumer must authenticate the target
-- producer before an admission means anything — this entry never invents a
-- target, but it believes the ones it is handed.
--
-- INERT: nothing consumes this outcome. Every Fenel-bodied call fences for want
-- of a summary, so an admitted body in this slice is one that calls nothing but
-- host implementations with ground arguments.
@label "Validation observation fence"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the public entry of the quantified-observation fence. Takes ONE FROZEN REQUEST carrying the raw body, the DECLARED parameter types, the quantifier vector, the frozen call targets, the execution mode and the invalidation identity; ORIGINATES every parameter's provenance and the scope's ordinal set itself; and reports either the accumulated fence set (not guaranteed exhaustive: two call-gate rules return early, which is fail-closed) or the body's result provenance with the profile set the verdict covers. 3b took prebuilt provenance, which made the shell-completeness invariant a contract on the caller — a shell omitting a tainted payload read as ground and admitted every deep observation of it. Still ATTESTED and not authenticated here: the declared types, the quantifier vector, the frozen targets and the identity hashes. INERT: no checker, decider, kernel, or dispatch path consumes this."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobAnalyze : (request: ObsRequest) -> ObsOutcome
vobAnalyze request =
  let ordinals = vobScopeOrdinals request.quantified 0 []
  let afterRequest = vobRequestIssues request []
  let afterMode = vobModeGate request.lowering request.evaluator afterRequest
  let afterAnalysedLabel = vobProfileLabelGate request.lowering request.analysedProfiles "the analysed" afterMode
  let afterLabel = vobProfileLabelGate request.lowering request.requiredProfiles "the required" afterAnalysedLabel
  let seeded = vobProfileGate request.analysedProfiles request.requiredProfiles afterLabel
  let binds = vobOriginateParams request.params request.quantified ordinals []
  let env = { callerId = request.callerId, targets = request.targets, ordinals = ordinals, binds = binds, profiles = request.analysedProfiles }
  let st = vobWalk request.body [] env seeded
  if eq (length st.reasons) 0
  then ObsAdmitted { prov = st.prov, profiles = request.analysedProfiles }
  else ObsFenced { reasons = st.reasons }

-- vobAnalyzeFromProvenance — ANALYSIS-INTERNAL, NOT the public entry.
--
-- It accepts PRE-ORIGINATED provenance and a caller-stated ordinal set, which
-- is exactly what 3d-D1 removed from `vobAnalyze`. It exists because the
-- algebra battery has to drive shell and opaque scrutinees through the walker
-- directly — the public entry cannot produce a shell, by design, so without
-- this the shell rules would be untestable end to end.
--
-- IT CARRIES NO JUDGMENT AUTHORITY. What keeps that true is not the name: it is
-- the phase-4 static gate, which proves no Fenel source and no production
-- TypeScript outside this module references any `vob*` function. A consumer
-- wired to this entry instead of `vobAnalyze` would reopen the caller-supplied
-- provenance hole in full, so the reachability gate is a precondition of the
-- whole group and not an inertness detail.
@label "observe: analyze from provenance"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — ANALYSIS-INTERNAL entry taking PRE-ORIGINATED parameter provenance and a caller-stated ordinal set, which is exactly what the public entry stopped accepting. It exists so the algebra battery can drive shell and opaque scrutinees through the walker directly, since the public entry cannot produce a shell by design. It carries NO judgment authority, and what keeps that true is the phase-4 static reachability gate, not the name: a consumer wired here instead of vobAnalyze would reopen the caller-supplied provenance hole in full."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobAnalyzeFromProvenance : (callerId: String) -> (body: (JsonLogic Any)) -> (params: List ObsBind) -> (ordinals: List Nat) -> (targets: List ObsCallTarget) -> (analysedProfiles: List String) -> (requiredProfiles: List String) -> ObsOutcome
vobAnalyzeFromProvenance callerId body params ordinals targets analysedProfiles requiredProfiles =
  let env = { callerId = callerId, targets = targets, ordinals = ordinals, binds = params, profiles = analysedProfiles }
  let seeded = vobProfileGate analysedProfiles requiredProfiles []
  let st = vobWalk body [] env seeded
  if eq (length st.reasons) 0
  then ObsAdmitted { prov = st.prov, profiles = analysedProfiles }
  else ObsFenced { reasons = st.reasons }

-- =========================================================================
-- the design-review repairs (3b design review, gpt-5.6-sol ultra 2026-07-26)
--
-- Each function below closes a finding the review raised against the plan. They
-- are grouped here rather than scattered so the disposition stays auditable
-- against `notes/phase-4-slice-3b-codex-design-review.md`.
-- =========================================================================

@label "observe: env-path op"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the missing / missing_some transfer. Their arguments are raw PATH NAMES, not values: the runtime resolves each name in the DATA CONTEXT and compares the resulting VALUE against null, undefined and the empty string (json-logic.ts:1628-1633), so a clean literal argument can still observe a κ-typed binding. Every literal path is resolved through the abstract environment and deep-observed; a computed or nested path abstains."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobEnvPathOp : (channel: String) -> (argList: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobEnvPathOp channel argList path env acc =
  if eq channel "missing_some"
  then vobStateOf PvClean (vobEnvPathCarrier channel (ifNthArg argList 1) path env acc)
  else vobStateOf PvClean (vobEnvPaths channel argList path env acc 1)

-- SLICE 3e — `missing_some` HAS A DIFFERENT SLOT LAYOUT. Raw slot 0 is the
-- numeric THRESHOLD, slot 1 is the key carrier, and trailing slots are
-- ignored. Reading slot 0 as a path made every well-formed
-- `{missing_some: [1, ["x"]]}` abstain on a number that is not a path at all.
-- The wrapper flatten is already consumed by `missing([keys], data)`, so the
-- carrier's own items are the paths with no further flatten left.
@label "observe: env path carrier"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3e - the missing_some key carrier at raw slot 1. Slot 0 is the numeric threshold, not a path, and the wrapper flatten is already consumed by the inner missing call, so the carrier's items are the paths with no flatten remaining. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobEnvPathCarrier : (channel: String) -> (node: (JsonLogic Any)) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: a) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobEnvPathCarrier channel node path env acc = case node of
  JlArray { items = xs } -> vobEnvPaths channel xs path env acc 0
  _ -> appendItem (vobAbstain "the missing_some key carrier is not a literal list, so the runtime coerces it into a single joined string key this analysis cannot model") acc

@label "observe: env paths"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — resolve each raw path-name argument through the abstract environment and deep-observe the value it names; a non-literal path abstains. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobEnvPaths : (channel: String) -> (items: a) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> (flattensLeft: Nat) -> List ValidationReason
vobEnvPaths channel items path env acc flattensLeft = case head items of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just item ->
    let next = case item of
          JlString { value = name } -> vobEnvPathName channel name path env acc
          JlArray { items = xs } ->
            if eq flattensLeft 0
            then appendItem (vobAbstain "path-name operator argument nests deeper than the runtime's single flatten, so the surviving array coerces to a joined string key this analysis cannot model") acc
            else vobEnvPaths channel xs path env acc (sub flattensLeft 1)
          _ -> appendItem (vobAbstain "path-name operator argument is not a literal name; the runtime coerces it with String(), producing a key this analysis cannot model") acc
    vobEnvPaths channel (eufRest items) path env next flattensLeft

@label "observe: env path name"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — deep-observe the value one raw path name resolves to in the abstract environment. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobEnvPathName : (channel: String) -> (name: String) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: a) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobEnvPathName channel name path env acc =
  let st = vobVarNamed name path env acc
  vobObserveDeep channel st.prov path st.reasons

-- FINDING 4c — the `$` APPLICATION head has a DIFFERENT layout from the ordinary
-- call form: the callee is at index 1 and the actuals begin at index 2
-- (json-logic.ts:2436-2439). Treating index 0 as the callee, as the generic call
-- skeleton does, mislabels one position. The form fences either way (the callee
-- is a VALUE, so no frozen target can describe it), but the callee is walked at
-- `VpsCallee` and the actuals at `VpsArg` so no nested observation inside either
-- is lost or misattributed.
@label "observe: dollar call"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the $ application head, whose layout differs from the ordinary call form: the callee is at index 1 and the actuals begin at index 2 (json-logic.ts:2436-2439). The form fences because the callee is a VALUE, but the callee is walked at VpsCallee and the actuals at VpsArg so no nested observation is lost or misattributed."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobDollarCall : (layout: FdcCallLayout) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (env: b) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> ObsState
vobDollarCall layout path env acc =
  let cst = vobWalk layout.calleeNode (appendItem VpsCallee path) env acc
  let seq = vobWalkSlots layout.slots path env cst.reasons []
  vobStateOf (vobUnknownProv env.ordinals) (appendItem (RsnDynamicOrReflectiveUse { useId = "$", detail = "the $ application head applies a callee VALUE, so no frozen target can describe it" }) seq.reasons)

-- FINDING 9 (HIGH) — a ctx-native has an AMBIENT input channel the explicit
-- argument list does not cover: it receives the whole `EvaluateContext`
-- (json-logic.ts:2370-2377), and evaluator strategies park caller data in that
-- context (`_localData`). So "every explicit argument is ground" is NOT a proof
-- that a ctx-native cannot see a κ-typed value.
--
-- Strict v1: a ctx-native branch fences whenever ANY rigid is live in the check
-- scope, regardless of what was passed explicitly. Naming the branch
-- `CtxNative` is not positive proof; a reviewed per-native context-footprint
-- attestation would be, and it does not exist. The `tier` field carries the
-- POST-FLATTEN winning native-map coordinate, so the ctx map is identified
-- exactly rather than guessed from the origin tag.
--
-- FINDING 6 (HIGH) - the NAMED-ARGUMENT hazard is REAL and the review's
-- diagnosis is right, but its proposed remedy (abstain on every namedish call)
-- is both unsound-SHAPED and unnecessary, and working the mechanism shows why.
--
-- Unsound-shaped: namedishness is a property of the EVALUATED argument, not of
-- the raw AST. `maybeReorderNamedArgs` (json-logic.ts:2059-2147) receives
-- evaluated values, so a raw `{var: "x"}` - a single-key plain object with no
-- `$` key - looks namedish to any AST-shaped detector while actually evaluating
-- to whatever `x` is bound to. Detecting it from the raw arguments therefore
-- fences ordinary calls and still misses the real cases.
--
-- Unnecessary: THE ARITY GATE SUBSUMES IT. The reorder fires ONLY when
-- `args.length === 1` (json-logic.ts:2069). Two cases:
--   * the callee's arity is also 1. Then the record's keys must be exactly its
--     one formal, the reorder yields exactly one argument, and index 0 still
--     maps to a provenance that DOMINATES what the callee receives - the record
--     shell's slots carry the field's taint by the completeness invariant. Every
--     downstream use (the observed-input check, the branch check, the output
--     derivation) is an over-approximation, which is the safe direction.
--   * the arity differs. Then a reorder can drop, reorder or SYNTHESIZE
--     arguments - and `supplied` differs from `arity`, which `vobArityGate`
--     already fences.
-- So no namedish rule is needed, and adding one would only lose coverage.
-- `vobNamedish` is retained as a DETECTOR, pinned by the subsumption test.
-- FINDING 4b + FINDING 5 (CRITICAL) — ARITY IS A GATE, in BOTH directions, and
-- neither direction is a wrapper detail.
--
--  * OVER-application creates a SECOND, UNGATED call: after a Fenel body or a
--    closure returns, the runtime tests whether the RESULT is callable and, if
--    so, applies the leftover arguments to it (json-logic.ts:2204-2211 and
--    2404-2410). That eta tail enters a callee this gate never saw. The sibling
--    ledger fences exactly this tail (`VusOver`), and strict v1 keeps the fence
--    rather than trying to gate a callee whose identity is a returned value.
--  * UNDER-application produces a `{__fenelPartial}` carrying the collected
--    argument VALUES (json-logic.ts:2358-2364), whose later application — with
--    the collected arguments PREPENDED (json-logic.ts:2167-2170) — likewise
--    happens somewhere this analysis does not see.
--
-- So a call is gateable only at EXACT arity.
@label "observe: arity gate"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — arity is a gate in BOTH directions. Over-application creates a SECOND ungated call: the runtime tests whether a returned value is callable and applies the leftover arguments to it (json-logic.ts:2204-2211, 2404-2410). Under-application produces a partial carrying the collected argument values, whose later application prepends them somewhere this analysis never sees. So a call is gateable only at exact arity."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobArityGate : (t: ObsCallTarget) -> (supplied: Nat) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobArityGate t supplied path acc =
  if lt supplied t.arity
  then appendItem (RsnUnsupportedPartialApplication { useId = t.rawKey }) acc
  else if lt t.arity supplied
  then appendItem (RsnUnsupportedPartialApplication { useId = t.rawKey }) (appendItem (vobAbstain "over-application eta-applies the leftover arguments to the RESULT, entering a callee this gate never saw") acc)
  else acc

-- FINDING 9 (HIGH) — a ctx-native has an AMBIENT input channel the explicit
-- argument list does not cover: it receives the whole `EvaluateContext`
-- (json-logic.ts:2370-2377), and evaluator strategies park caller data in that
-- context (`_localData`). So "every explicit argument is ground" is NOT a proof
-- that a ctx-native cannot see a κ-typed value.
--
-- Strict v1: a ctx-native branch fences whenever ANY rigid is live in the check
-- scope, regardless of what was passed explicitly. Naming the branch
-- `CtxNative` is not positive proof; a reviewed per-native context-footprint
-- attestation would be, and it does not exist. The `tier` field carries the
-- POST-FLATTEN winning native-map coordinate, so the ctx map is identified
-- exactly rather than guessed from the origin tag.
--
-- FINDING 6 (HIGH) - the NAMED-ARGUMENT hazard is REAL and the review's
-- diagnosis is right, but its proposed remedy (abstain on every namedish call)
-- is both unsound-SHAPED and unnecessary, and working the mechanism shows why.
--
-- Unsound-shaped: namedishness is a property of the EVALUATED argument, not of
-- the raw AST. `maybeReorderNamedArgs` (json-logic.ts:2059-2147) receives
-- evaluated values, so a raw `{var: "x"}` - a single-key plain object with no
-- `$` key - looks namedish to any AST-shaped detector while actually evaluating
-- to whatever `x` is bound to. Detecting it from the raw arguments therefore
-- fences ordinary calls and still misses the real cases.
--
-- Unnecessary: THE ARITY GATE SUBSUMES IT. The reorder fires ONLY when
-- `args.length === 1` (json-logic.ts:2069). Two cases:
--   * the callee's arity is also 1. Then the record's keys must be exactly its
--     one formal, the reorder yields exactly one argument, and index 0 still
--     maps to a provenance that DOMINATES what the callee receives - the record
--     shell's slots carry the field's taint by the completeness invariant. Every
--     downstream use (the observed-input check, the branch check, the output
--     derivation) is an over-approximation, which is the safe direction.
--   * the arity differs. Then a reorder can drop, reorder or SYNTHESIZE
--     arguments - and `supplied` differs from `arity`, which `vobArityGate`
--     already fences.
-- So no namedish rule is needed, and adding one would only lose coverage.
-- `vobNamedish` is retained as a DETECTOR, pinned by the subsumption test.
@label "observe: ambient gate"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the channel the explicit argument list does not cover: a ctx-native receives the whole EvaluateContext (json-logic.ts:2370-2377), in which evaluator strategies park caller data, so ground explicit arguments do not prove it cannot see a κ-typed value. It fences whenever any rigid is live in scope. The named-argument hazard is NOT gated here — the arity gate subsumes it; see the note above vobNamedish."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobAmbientGate : (t: ObsCallTarget) -> (liveRigids: List Nat) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobAmbientGate t liveRigids path acc =
  if vobIsCtxTier t.tier
  then vobObserveDeep "ctx-native-ambient-context" (vobOpaqueOf liveRigids) path acc
  else acc

@label "observe: isCtxTier"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — does the frozen POST-FLATTEN native-map coordinate name the ctx-aware map (the one whose implementations receive the whole EvaluateContext)? Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobIsCtxTier : (tier: String) -> Boolean
vobIsCtxTier tier =
  if eq tier "nativeImplsCtx" then true else eq tier "both"

-- FINDING 3 (CRITICAL) — a summary that records only OUTPUT dependency cannot
-- stop taint laundering through a formal the callee declared as `Any`:
--
--     inspect : Any -> Boolean       inspect y = isArray y
--     bad : ∀a. a -> Boolean         bad x = inspect x
--
-- Analysed in isolation, `inspect`'s `y` starts clean, so an output-only summary
-- says nothing derives from the input — and the κ actual at the call site would
-- be admitted even though `inspect` observes it. Values cross a call boundary
-- UNCHANGED (`invokeFunction` binds actuals straight to formal names,
-- json-logic.ts:2394-2399), so the callee's own quantifiers are irrelevant to
-- what it can observe.
--
-- The repair is a declared `observesFrom` relation: the parameter indices the
-- callee OBSERVES, checked against the ACTUAL provenance at those positions. A
-- summary must therefore be proved with every formal SYMBOLICALLY tainted —
-- never in an environment where an `Any` formal happened to be clean — and
-- `outputDerivesFrom` must be derived the same way. 3c/3d own producing such
-- summaries; this gate owns refusing any that does not carry the relation.
-- FINDING 3 (CRITICAL) — a summary that records only OUTPUT dependency cannot
-- stop taint laundering through a formal the callee declared as `Any`:
--
--     inspect : Any -> Boolean       inspect y = isArray y
--     bad : ∀a. a -> Boolean         bad x = inspect x
--
-- Analysed in isolation, `inspect`'s `y` starts clean, so an output-only summary
-- says nothing derives from the input — and the κ actual at the call site would
-- be admitted even though `inspect` observes it. Values cross a call boundary
-- UNCHANGED (`invokeFunction` binds actuals straight to formal names,
-- json-logic.ts:2394-2399), so the callee's own quantifiers are irrelevant to
-- what it can observe.
--
-- The repair is a declared `observesFrom` relation: the parameter indices the
-- callee OBSERVES, checked against the ACTUAL provenance at those positions. A
-- summary must therefore be proved with every formal SYMBOLICALLY tainted —
-- never in an environment where an `Any` formal happened to be clean — and
-- `outputDerivesFrom` must be derived the same way. 3c/3d own producing such
-- summaries; this gate owns refusing any that does not carry the relation.
@label "observe: observed-input gate"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the repair for taint laundering through an Any-typed formal. A summary recording only OUTPUT dependency cannot stop it: values cross a call boundary unchanged (json-logic.ts:2394-2399), so a callee that observes a formal it declared as Any observes the κ actual regardless of its own quantifiers. The summary must declare observesFrom — the parameter indices it OBSERVES — and this gate checks the ACTUAL provenance at those positions, so a summary proved in an environment where an Any formal happened to be clean cannot authorize anything."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobObservedInputGate : (s: ObsProvSummary) -> (argProvs: List ObsProv) -> (path: List UsePathSeg) -> (acc: List ValidationReason) -> List ValidationReason
vobObservedInputGate s argProvs path acc = case head s.observesFrom of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just i ->
    let next = case vobNthProv argProvs i of
          Nothing -> appendItem (vobAbstain "summary names an observed parameter index past the analysed argument list") acc
          Just p -> vobObserveDeep "callee-observed-input" p path acc
    vobObservedInputGate (vobDropObserved s) argProvs path next

@label "observe: drop observed"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the summary with its first observed-parameter index consumed. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobDropObserved : (s: ObsProvSummary) -> ObsProvSummary
vobDropObserved s =
  ObsProvSummary
    { targetId = s.targetId, schemeHash = s.schemeHash, origin = s.origin, profile = s.profile, version = s.version, paramCount = s.paramCount, formals = s.formals, observesFrom = eufRest s.observesFrom, outputDerivesFrom = s.outputDerivesFrom, outputIntrinsicRigids = s.outputIntrinsicRigids, invalidationKey = s.invalidationKey }

-- FINDING 2 (CRITICAL) — A TYPE CONSTRUCTOR'S NAME IS NOT A REPRESENTATION
-- PROOF, so "a known former applied to κ originates a shell" is UNSOUND as
-- stated. `$tagged` is an ERASED phantom wrapper (types.ts:456) and `$refined`
-- is likewise transparent: shape checking descends to the value/base type, so
-- `Tagged κ P` has κ's RUNTIME REPRESENTATION, not a `Tagged` shell. A body
-- matching such a value against a `$tag` pattern could then distinguish
-- `a = Maybe Number` from `a = Number` while a shell-originated M5 admitted it.
-- `$opaque` is no safer: its representation comes from per-target `Reprable`
-- instances (types.ts:468), while dispatch observes the ACTUAL JS
-- boolean/number/string/array/`$tag` shape (dispatch.fenel:165-175).
--
-- So origination consumes a CLOSED REPRESENTATION DESCRIPTOR (`ObsRepr`, 3d-D1),
-- never a type head. 3b spelled the descriptor as an OPEN record
-- (`{witnessedShape, transparent, slots}`), which meant "the descriptor" was
-- whatever a caller chose to pass; the ADT is the shape the ledger row always
-- described. `RprGround` yields `PvClean`, `RprOpaque` the opaque atom over its
-- ordinals, `RprTransparent` its INNER's provenance recursively (3d-D2 — 3b
-- returned the opaque atom here because no inner was supplied), and only
-- `RprShell` a shell.
--
-- THE COMPLETENESS INVARIANT. `vobIsGround` recurses only through MODELLED
-- slots, so a shell whose slots omit a tainted payload would read as ground.
-- Every shell this module builds carries its complete taint (an array literal's
-- element join, a record literal's every field, a constructor's both payload
-- readings, a closure's whole capture), and a descriptor supplied here MUST too.
-- A future shell producer that models only some of a payload breaks the
-- invariant and must not be added.
--
-- TWO DEFENCES ON A SHELL DESCRIPTOR, AND NEITHER IS A COMPLETENESS PROOF.
-- Duplicate slot keys DEGRADE the descriptor, because `vobSlotLookup` takes the
-- first match while `vobRigidsOf` unions them all: a duplicate pair could put a
-- CLEAN slot in front of the tainted one carrying the same key, passing the
-- coverage floor while every projection read the clean answer. And the ordinal
-- floor below is a FLOOR, not a proof — it asks only that the declared ordinals
-- occur SOMEWHERE in the shell, so a shell with a clean real payload and a
-- bogus extra slot still passes. Both are recorded as such in `obs.shell.complete`.
-- FINDING 2 (CRITICAL) — A TYPE CONSTRUCTOR'S NAME IS NOT A REPRESENTATION
-- PROOF, so "a known former applied to κ originates a shell" is UNSOUND as
-- stated. `$tagged` is an ERASED phantom wrapper (types.ts:456) and `$refined`
-- is likewise transparent: shape checking descends to the value/base type, so
-- `Tagged κ P` has κ's RUNTIME REPRESENTATION, not a `Tagged` shell. A body
-- matching such a value against a `$tag` pattern could then distinguish
-- `a = Maybe Number` from `a = Number` while a shell-originated M5 admitted it.
-- `$opaque` is no safer: its representation comes from per-target `Reprable`
-- instances (types.ts:468), while dispatch observes the ACTUAL JS
-- boolean/number/string/array/`$tag` shape (dispatch.fenel:165-175).
--
-- So origination consumes a CLOSED REPRESENTATION DESCRIPTOR (`ObsRepr`, 3d-D1),
-- never a type head. 3b spelled the descriptor as an OPEN record
-- (`{witnessedShape, transparent, slots}`), which meant "the descriptor" was
-- whatever a caller chose to pass; the ADT is the shape the ledger row always
-- described. `RprGround` yields `PvClean`, `RprOpaque` the opaque atom over its
-- ordinals, `RprTransparent` its INNER's provenance recursively (3d-D2 — 3b
-- returned the opaque atom here because no inner was supplied), and only
-- `RprShell` a shell.
--
-- THE COMPLETENESS INVARIANT. `vobIsGround` recurses only through MODELLED
-- slots, so a shell whose slots omit a tainted payload would read as ground.
-- Every shell this module builds carries its complete taint (an array literal's
-- element join, a record literal's every field, a constructor's both payload
-- readings, a closure's whole capture), and a descriptor supplied here MUST too.
-- A future shell producer that models only some of a payload breaks the
-- invariant and must not be added.
--
-- TWO DEFENCES ON A SHELL DESCRIPTOR, AND NEITHER IS A COMPLETENESS PROOF.
-- Duplicate slot keys DEGRADE the descriptor, because `vobSlotLookup` takes the
-- first match while `vobRigidsOf` unions them all: a duplicate pair could put a
-- CLEAN slot in front of the tainted one carrying the same key, passing the
-- coverage floor while every projection read the clean answer. And the ordinal
-- floor below is a FLOOR, not a proof — it asks only that the declared ordinals
-- occur SOMEWHERE in the shell, so a shell with a clean real payload and a
-- bogus extra slot still passes. Both are recorded as such in `obs.shell.complete`.
@label "observe: repr to prov"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — originate one parameter's provenance from the CLOSED ObsRepr descriptor rather than a type head (3b took an open record). A type constructor's name is not a representation proof: $tagged is an erased phantom wrapper and $refined is transparent, so such a type has its INNER value's runtime representation, and $opaque's representation comes from per-target Reprable instances while dispatch observes the actual JS shape. RprGround yields PvClean; RprOpaque the opaque atom; RprTransparent its INNER's provenance RECURSIVELY (3b returned the opaque atom because no inner was supplied); only RprShell a shell — degraded to opaque on duplicate slot keys or when its own ordinals do not cover the scope's."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobReprToProv : (r: ObsRepr) -> (ordinals: List Nat) -> ObsProv
vobReprToProv r ordinals = case r of
  RprGround -> PvClean
  RprOpaque { ordinals = os } -> vobOpaqueOf os
  RprTransparent { inner = inner } -> vobReprToProv inner ordinals
  RprShell { shape = shape, slots = sl } ->
    if not (vobSlotKeysDistinct sl [])
    then vobOpaqueOf ordinals
    else
      let shell = vobShellOf shape (vobReprSlots sl ordinals [])
      if vobCoversOrdinals (vobRigidsOf shell) ordinals
      then shell
      else vobOpaqueOf ordinals

@label "observe: repr slots"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — project a descriptor's payload slots into provenance slots, recursively. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobReprSlots : (sl: List ObsReprSlot) -> (ordinals: List Nat) -> (acc: List ObsProvSlot) -> List ObsProvSlot
vobReprSlots sl ordinals acc = case head sl of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just s -> vobReprSlots (eufRest sl) ordinals (appendItem (ObsProvSlot { key = s.key, prov = vobReprToProv s.repr ordinals }) acc)

@label "observe: slot keys distinct"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — are a descriptor's payload slot keys pairwise distinct? Load-bearing rather than tidiness: vobSlotLookup takes the FIRST slot at a key while vobRigidsOf unions ALL of them, so a duplicate pair can pass the ordinal-coverage floor on a tainted slot while every projection reads a clean one in front of it. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobSlotKeysDistinct : (sl: List ObsReprSlot) -> (seen: List String) -> Boolean
vobSlotKeysDistinct sl seen = case head sl of
  Nothing -> true
  Just s ->
    if vobNameIn seen s.key
    then false
    else vobSlotKeysDistinct (eufRest sl) (appendItem s.key seen)

@label "observe: covers ordinals"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — does a provenance's own ordinal set cover every ordinal the scope says this parameter carries? The FLOOR on an originated shell (3d: a floor, explicitly not a proof): a shell descriptor is an attestation the ADT cannot verify, so a witnessed shape whose slots declare FEWER rigids than the scope has must degrade to the opaque atom rather than be taken at its word. It does NOT establish slot completeness — a shell with a clean real payload and a bogus extra slot still passes — and for a `Maybe a` under `forall a b.` it demands `b` too, which over-fences. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobCoversOrdinals : (have: List Nat) -> (need: List Nat) -> Boolean
vobCoversOrdinals have need = case head need of
  Nothing -> true
  Just o -> if vobHasOrdinal have o then vobCoversOrdinals have (eufRest need) else false

-- =========================================================================
-- 3d-D1 — DERIVING a descriptor from a declared type
--
-- This is the Fenel port of the census's `bareQuantifiedOrdinalOf` /
-- `mentionsQuantified` / parameter-origination loop, and it is now the ONE
-- authority: the census calls it instead of carrying its own copy.
--
-- IT NEVER WITNESSES A SHELL. A declared type is not a representation proof
-- (finding 2), so the answer is `RprGround` or `RprOpaque` and nothing else.
-- The precision this gives up is real — `Maybe κ` originates as the opaque atom
-- rather than as a `Maybe` shell over an opaque payload, so a `$tag`
-- discrimination on it fences where a witnessed shell would admit — and giving
-- it up is the point: the shell is what needs a witness.
--
-- THREE THINGS DEGRADE TO "OPAQUE OVER EVERY ORDINAL IN SCOPE", and each is a
-- case where answering GROUND would be a false admission rather than a loss of
-- precision:
--
--  1. A `$el` NODE ANYWHERE. That is how the compatibility encoding spells a
--     higher-kinded application: `f a` is `{$el: {call: ["f", {$var: "a"}]}}`
--     — the head `f` is a bare STRING, and the fact that it denotes a
--     quantified variable lives in the authoritative `TypeScheme.applications`
--     sidecar as `headVarId` (`types.ts`'s `SchemeApplicationBase`, and
--     `engine-bodies-dispatch.ts` warns against rediscovering it by walking the
--     compatibility body). A `$var` scan therefore MISSES the head's ordinal
--     entirely, and for `f Number` there is no `$var` at all — it would answer
--     GROUND for a parameter whose runtime shape changes with `f`. Degrading on
--     any `$el` covers that without consulting the sidecar, at the cost of
--     over-fencing ordinary dependent types. Live instances exist
--     (`algebra:liftZip2`'s `x : f a`, `algebra:vecIndex`'s `v : Vec n a`).
--  2. A `$var` NAMING NO QUANTIFIER. Unknown is not ground.
--  3. FUEL EXHAUSTION. A depth cap that silently stops walking would miss a
--     deep `$var` and answer GROUND — the census's TypeScript copy caps at
--     depth 12 and returns false, which is exactly that bug. Here exhaustion
--     degrades.
-- =========================================================================

@label "observe: quantifier ordinal"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the ORDINAL (index in the scheme's quantifier vector) of the quantifier with this SOURCE spelling, if any. Matched on sourceName ALONE: the generated id namespace (q0, q1, …) is deliberately not tried, because `collide : a -> q0 -> a` is legal source and matching either slot would resolve {$var: \"q0\"} to the wrong binder. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobQuantifierOrdinal : (qs: List ObsQuantifier) -> (sourceName: String) -> (index: Nat) -> Maybe Nat
vobQuantifierOrdinal qs sourceName index = case head qs of
  Nothing -> Nothing
  Just q ->
    if eq q.sourceName sourceName
    then Just index
    else vobQuantifierOrdinal (eufRest qs) sourceName (add index 1)

@label "observe: scan type"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — walk a marshalled declared type collecting every quantifier ordinal it mentions, and recording whether the walk must DEGRADE to the whole scope (a $el application head whose quantified identity lives in the scheme sidecar, a $var naming no quantifier, or fuel exhaustion). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobScanType : (node: (JsonLogic Any)) -> (quantified: List ObsQuantifier) -> (fuel: Nat) -> (acc: a) -> a
vobScanType node quantified fuel acc =
  if eq fuel 0
  then { ordinals = acc.ordinals, degrade = true }
  else if acc.degrade
  then acc
  else case node of
    JlArray { items = xs } -> vobScanItems xs quantified (sub fuel 1) acc
    JlObject { fields = fs } -> vobScanFields fs quantified (sub fuel 1) acc
    JlTagged { fields = fs } -> vobScanFields fs quantified (sub fuel 1) acc
    _ -> acc

@label "observe: scan items"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the declared-type scan over a marshalled item list. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
-- WIDTH IS BOUNDED TOO, and the reason is not tidiness. Depth fuel alone leaves
-- the SIBLING folds unbounded: a valid declared type with a very wide former (a
-- ten-thousand-element `$tuple` reproduces it) drives one interpreter frame per
-- sibling and overflows the host stack — a totality/availability defect, and the
-- one failure mode that is neither a fence nor an admission. Exhausting the
-- sibling budget DEGRADES and RETURNS, so the fold stops rather than walking the
-- remaining siblings to hand each one an already-degraded accumulator.
vobScanSiblingBudget : (unit: Any) -> Nat
vobScanSiblingBudget unit = 1024

@label "observe: scan items"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the declared-type scan over a marshalled item list, bounded in WIDTH as well as depth: depth fuel alone leaves the sibling fold unbounded, and a very wide former drives one interpreter frame per sibling and overflows the host stack. Exhausting the sibling budget degrades and returns. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobScanItems : (xs: a) -> (quantified: List ObsQuantifier) -> (fuel: Nat) -> (acc: b) -> b
vobScanItems xs quantified fuel acc = vobScanItemsWide xs quantified fuel (vobScanSiblingBudget 0) acc

@label "observe: scan items wide"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the width-bounded item fold of the declared-type scan. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobScanItemsWide : (xs: a) -> (quantified: List ObsQuantifier) -> (fuel: Nat) -> (width: Nat) -> (acc: b) -> b
vobScanItemsWide xs quantified fuel width acc = case head xs of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just x ->
    if eq width 0
    then { ordinals = acc.ordinals, degrade = true }
    else vobScanItemsWide (eufRest xs) quantified fuel (sub width 1) (vobScanType x quantified fuel acc)

@label "observe: scan fields"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the declared-type scan over a marshalled field list: each field's NAME is classified, then its value is walked. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobScanFields : (fs: a) -> (quantified: List ObsQuantifier) -> (fuel: Nat) -> (acc: b) -> b
vobScanFields fs quantified fuel acc = vobScanFieldsWide fs quantified fuel (vobScanSiblingBudget 0) acc

@label "observe: scan fields wide"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the width-bounded field fold of the declared-type scan; each field's NAME is classified, then its value is walked. Exhausting the sibling budget degrades and returns, so a very wide record cannot drive the host stack over. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobScanFieldsWide : (fs: a) -> (quantified: List ObsQuantifier) -> (fuel: Nat) -> (width: Nat) -> (acc: b) -> b
vobScanFieldsWide fs quantified fuel width acc = case head fs of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just f ->
    if eq width 0
    then { ordinals = acc.ordinals, degrade = true }
    else
      let here = vobScanFieldHead f quantified acc
      let deeper = vobScanType f.value quantified fuel here
      vobScanFieldsWide (eufRest fs) quantified fuel (sub width 1) deeper

@label "observe: scan field head"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — classify ONE field name of a marshalled declared type: $el degrades (a higher-kinded application's head identity is in the scheme sidecar, not here), a $var naming a quantifier contributes its ordinal, and a $var naming nothing — or holding a non-literal — degrades. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobScanFieldHead : (f: a) -> (quantified: List ObsQuantifier) -> (acc: b) -> b
vobScanFieldHead f quantified acc =
  if eq f.name "$el"
  then { ordinals = acc.ordinals, degrade = true }
  else if not (eq f.name "$var")
  then acc
  else case f.value of
    JlString { value = s } -> case vobQuantifierOrdinal quantified s 0 of
      Nothing -> { ordinals = acc.ordinals, degrade = true }
      Just o -> { ordinals = vobAddOrdinal acc.ordinals o, degrade = acc.degrade }
    _ -> { ordinals = acc.ordinals, degrade = true }

@label "observe: derive repr"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — derive one parameter's CLOSED representation descriptor from its DECLARED TYPE. Answers RprGround or RprOpaque and never a shell, because a declared type is not a representation proof. Degrades to opaque over EVERY ordinal in scope on a $el node (the compatibility spelling of a higher-kinded application, whose head identity lives in the TypeScheme.applications sidecar this traversal does not consult — so a $var scan alone answers GROUND for `f Number`, a false admission), on a $var naming no quantifier, and on fuel exhaustion."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobDeriveRepr : (declared: (JsonLogic Any)) -> (quantified: List ObsQuantifier) -> (scopeOrdinals: List Nat) -> ObsRepr
vobDeriveRepr declared quantified scopeOrdinals =
  let scan = vobScanType declared quantified 64 { ordinals = [], degrade = false }
  if scan.degrade
  then RprOpaque { ordinals = scopeOrdinals }
  else if eq (length scan.ordinals) 0
  then RprGround
  else RprOpaque { ordinals = scan.ordinals }

@label "observe: scope ordinals"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the check scope's quantifier ordinals, [0 .. n-1] over the scheme's quantifier vector. Derived from the vector rather than accepted from a caller: a caller-supplied ordinal set is a channel for making the scope look emptier than it is, and an empty scope makes every provenance clean. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobScopeOrdinals : (qs: List ObsQuantifier) -> (index: Nat) -> (acc: List Nat) -> List Nat
vobScopeOrdinals qs index acc = case head qs of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just q -> vobScopeOrdinals (eufRest qs) (add index 1) (appendItem index acc)

-- =========================================================================
-- 3d-D1 — the RAW-KEY HARVEST, likewise ported out of the census.
--
-- Every object key and call head reachable in a marshalled body. SYNTACTIC by
-- design: a key with no registry resolution simply has no frozen record, and
-- the gate reports that as an unresolved use rather than as an assumption.
-- `{call: [head, …]}` and `{method: [Class, name, …]}` put their heads as
-- literal STRINGS inside the argument list rather than as object keys, so those
-- two lists are scanned for string items as well.
-- =========================================================================

@label "observe: add name"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — add a spelling to a set of spellings (idempotent). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobAddName : (acc: List String) -> (n: String) -> List String
vobAddName acc n = if vobNameIn acc n then acc else appendItem n acc

@label "observe: is call head key"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — is this field name one whose ARGUMENT LIST carries a callee head as a literal string rather than as an object key (call, method)? Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobIsCallHeadKey : (name: String) -> Boolean
vobIsCallHeadKey name = if eq name "call" then true else eq name "method"

@label "observe: harvest raw keys"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — every object key and call head reachable in a marshalled raw body. Syntactic by design: a key with no registry resolution has no frozen call-target record, which the gate reports as an unresolved use rather than as an assumption. The call and method forms carry their heads as literal strings inside the argument list rather than as object keys, so those lists are scanned for string items too. Ported out of the census's TypeScript copy so origination and harvesting have ONE authority."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobHarvestRawKeys : (node: (JsonLogic Any)) -> (acc: List String) -> List String
vobHarvestRawKeys node acc = case node of
  JlArray { items = xs } -> vobHarvestItems xs acc
  JlObject { fields = fs } -> vobHarvestFields fs acc
  JlTagged { fields = fs } -> vobHarvestFields fs acc
  _ -> acc

@label "observe: harvest items"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the raw-key harvest over a marshalled item list. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobHarvestItems : (xs: a) -> (acc: List String) -> List String
vobHarvestItems xs acc = case head xs of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just x -> vobHarvestItems (eufRest xs) (vobHarvestRawKeys x acc)

@label "observe: harvest fields"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the raw-key harvest over a marshalled field list: the field NAME, then any literal callee head inside a call or method argument list, then the field value. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobHarvestFields : (fs: a) -> (acc: List String) -> List String
vobHarvestFields fs acc = case head fs of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just f ->
    let named = vobAddName acc f.name
    let heads = if vobIsCallHeadKey f.name then vobHarvestHeads f.value named else named
    vobHarvestFields (eufRest fs) (vobHarvestRawKeys f.value heads)

@label "observe: harvest heads"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — the literal string items of a call or method argument list, which is where those two forms carry their callee head. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobHarvestHeads : (value: (JsonLogic Any)) -> (acc: List String) -> List String
vobHarvestHeads value acc = case value of
  JlArray { items = xs } -> vobHarvestHeadItems xs acc
  _ -> acc

@label "observe: harvest head items"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — accumulate the literal string items of an argument list. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
@category "engine-internal"
vobHarvestHeadItems : (xs: a) -> (acc: List String) -> List String
vobHarvestHeadItems xs acc = case head xs of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just x ->
    let next = case x of
          JlString { value = s } -> vobAddName acc s
          _ -> acc
    vobHarvestHeadItems (eufRest xs) next

@label "observe: originate params"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3d — originate the whole parameter scope INSIDE the judgment: each declared parameter's provenance is derived from its declared type through the closed descriptor, in declaration order. This is what makes obs.shell.complete an enforced invariant on the public entry rather than a contract on the caller."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobOriginateParams : (ps: List ObsParam) -> (quantified: List ObsQuantifier) -> (ordinals: List Nat) -> (acc: List ObsBind) -> List ObsBind
vobOriginateParams ps quantified ordinals acc = case head ps of
  Nothing -> acc
  Just p ->
    let prov = vobReprToProv (vobDeriveRepr p.declared quantified ordinals) ordinals
    vobOriginateParams (eufRest ps) quantified ordinals (appendItem (ObsBind { name = p.name, prov = prov }) acc)

-- The NAMEDISH shape: exactly one argument that is a plain object with no
-- `$`-prefixed key - what `maybeReorderNamedArgs` may read as named fields
-- (json-logic.ts:2069-2091; a `$`-keyed record is a WIRE VALUE and is never
-- named args).
--
-- DETECTOR ONLY, NOT A GATE, for the subsumption reason recorded at
-- `vobAmbientGate`: the reorder fires only at `args.length === 1`, where either
-- the callee's arity is 1 (so index 0 maps to a provenance that dominates what
-- the callee receives) or `supplied` differs from `arity` (so `vobArityGate`
-- fences). It is also an AST-shaped test for a property of the EVALUATED
-- argument, so it reports true for a raw `{var: "x"}` - which is exactly why it
-- must not gate.
@label "observe: namedish"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — is this argument list the NAMEDISH shape maybeReorderNamedArgs may read as named fields: exactly one argument that is a plain object with no $-prefixed key (a $-keyed record is a wire value and is never named args, json-logic.ts:2069-2091)? DETECTOR ONLY — the arity gate subsumes the hazard, and this AST-shaped test reports true for a raw {var} whose evaluated value is not a record at all, so it must not gate."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobNamedish : (argList: a) -> Boolean
vobNamedish argList =
  if not (eq (length argList) 1)
  then false
  else case head argList of
    Nothing -> false
    Just only -> case only of
      JlObject { fields = fs } ->
        if eq (length fs) 0 then false else not (objectHasDollarPrefixedKey fs)
      _ -> false

-- FINDING 4d — the `method` form is NOT uniformly qualified dispatch. It has a
-- module-member direct-call branch, projected raw host methods are invoked
-- directly, and both qualified and bare dispatch retain live oracle-fallback
-- paths. So the form's key must identify the QUALIFIED target the way the
-- resolver's own position index does (`Class.name`, dispatch.fenel:334-336),
-- and the frozen record's `dispatchRoute` — not this walker's assumption —
-- decides whether the call reflects a dispatch argument at all. An absent record
-- is an unresolved use, and an unrecognized route abstains.
@label "observe: method key"
@description "signature-substrate Phase 4 slice 3b — the qualified key for a method form, built the way the resolver's own position index is (Class.name, dispatch.fenel:334-336). The method form is not uniformly qualified dispatch — it also has a module-member direct branch, directly-invoked projected host methods, and oracle-fallback paths — so the frozen record's dispatchRoute decides whether the call reflects a dispatch argument, not this walker."
@tags "engine" "validation" "observe" "signature-substrate" "phase-4"
vobMethodKey : (argList: a) -> (m: String) -> String
vobMethodKey argList m = case head argList of
  Nothing -> "«unresolvable-method-key»"
  Just clsNode -> case clsNode of
    JlString { value = cls } -> concat (concat cls ".") m
    _ -> "«unresolvable-method-key»"
